我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们一起出演过《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两个人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室娇娃。

8
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.300
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.680
Welcome to Sabre.
欢迎来到《赛博》。

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:43.380
Yes, it is Season 6, Episode 15, written by Jennifer Salata, known to us as Jen Salata, and directed by John Krasinski.
没错，这是第六季第十五集，由珍妮弗·萨拉塔（我们称她为珍·萨拉塔）编剧，约翰·卡拉辛斯基执导。

11
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.800
Yes, known to us as J.K.
是的，我们称他为 J.K.

12
00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.500
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

13
00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:48.400
John.
约翰。

14
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.340
Great job.
干得漂亮。

15
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.100
I loved this episode.
我很喜欢这一集。

16
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:52.760
I did, too.
我也是。

17
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.800
It was one of those sleeper ones that I hadn't watched in years.
这是一集我好几年没看过、差点漏掉的宝藏剧集。

18
00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.180
That I had forgotten about.
我都快忘光了。

19
00:00:57.220 --> 00:00:57.500
Yeah.
是的。

20
00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.140
And I was cracking up.
我当时笑得前仰后合。

21
00:00:59.340 --> 00:00:59.980
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

22
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.100
So many memories flooded back for me.
无数的回忆瞬间涌上心头。

23
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.680
All those daycare scenes.
所有那些托儿所的场景。

24
00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.820
Oh, they were so good.
哦，拍得太棒了。

25
00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:06.840
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

26
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.340
I can't wait to talk about them.
我迫不及待想聊聊它们了。

27
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.500
I can't wait to talk about them.
我迫不及待想聊聊它们了。

28
00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.520
And there's even more in the shooting draft that didn't make it in.
而且拍摄剧本里还有更多没播出的内容。

29
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.940
So we're going to share it all with you.
所以我们要把这些全部分享给你们。

30
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.560
Here's a summary.
以下是剧情概要。

31
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:22.420
Dunder Mifflin has officially been bought by a new company, Sabre.
邓德·米夫林正式被一家新公司“赛博”收购。

32
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:27.240
Gabe Lewis, the new director of sales, arrives in Scranton and brings with him
新任销售总监盖比·刘易斯抵达斯克兰顿，随身带来了一份

33
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:32.060
a list of changes and new company policies that do not sit well with Michael.
改革清单和新公司政策，这让迈克尔很不痛快。

34
00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.500
Michael seeks advice from a very unemployed David Wallace.
迈克尔向处于严重失业状态的大卫·华莱士寻求建议。

35
00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:42.780
Meanwhile, Pam and Jim tour a daycare center, and Aaron and Andy wait for the other to make
与此同时，帕姆和吉姆参观了一家托儿所，艾琳和安迪则在等待对方先迈出

36
00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.260
a move.
一步。

37
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.420
It is the most awkward courtship of two people.
这是两个人之间最尴尬的追求。

38
00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:51.100
I was yelling at the TV screen.
我都对着电视屏幕大喊了。

39
00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.480
I was like, one of you just asked the other one out.
我当时就像在说，你们俩谁赶紧约对方出去啊。

40
00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.700
They're making me crazy.
他们快把我急疯了。

41
00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:01.320
We have so much stuff to share in this episode.
这一集里有太多料要分享了。

42
00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.580
I mean, I hope we can get through it all.
我是说，希望我们能全聊完。

43
00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.940
We better get to it.
我们最好抓紧时间吧。

44
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:10.260
But before we do, folks, I want you to know Jenna's wearing a poofy flower on her lapel today.
但在我们开始之前，各位，我想让你们知道珍娜今天在翻领上戴了一朵蓬松的花。

45
00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.860
Okay, I'm trying this.
好吧，我在尝试这种风格。

46
00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.400
This is your book look.
这是你的新书造型。

47
00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.000
Oh, and our book is coming out in two weeks.
哦，我们的书两周后就要出版了。

48
00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.140
In two weeks.
还有两周。

49
00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.360
Our book is launching into the world, and we need a bunch of outfits, Angela.
我们的书就要问世了，我们需要准备一堆衣服，安吉拉。

50
00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:30.220
You know I've been spending weeks and weeks curating outfits because I am not naturally
你知道我花了好几周时间精心挑选服装，因为我天生就不是

51
00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:33.220
gifted in that area.
在这方面很有天赋。

52
00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:38.520
I never want you to stop trying to put together outfits because now every day, and I'm talking,
我从来不想让你停止尝试搭配衣服，因为现在每天，我是说，

53
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:44.000
I mean, almost every day, I get a picture of you in front of your closet, and you're
我的意思是，几乎每天，我都会收到一张你站在衣柜前的照片，然后你

54
00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.760
like, what about this?
会说，这件怎么样？

55
00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:45.500
I know.
我知道。

56
00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.080
And so here's the problem I'm having.
所以这就是我遇到的问题。

57
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:51.220
I declared that I was going to wear fakie flowers.
我宣称我要戴假花。

58
00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.400
You sure did.
你确实这么说了。

59
00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.860
You made a big declaration.
你发出了郑重的宣言。

60
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.220
And it's not working.
结果行不通。

61
00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.300
I'm wearing one today because I wanted you to see.
我今天戴着一个，因为我想让你看看。

62
00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.020
Hear me out.
听我说完。

63
00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:00.840
I'm going to stand up.
我要站起来了。

64
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:04.080
Well, I want you to see what I think is happening here.
嗯，我想让你看看我觉得这里发生了什么。

65
00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:08.260
And I know it's the striped shirt, but I think it's the fakie flower, too.
我知道是这件条纹衬衫的问题，但我也觉得是假花的问题。

66
00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.280
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

67
00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:09.720
Yeah.
好吧。

68
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:11.460
What does this remind you of?
这让你想起了什么？

69
00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:14.860
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

70
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.320
You look like a French mime.
你看起来像个法国哑剧演员。

71
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.080
I look like a Parisian mime.
我看起来像个巴黎哑剧演员。

72
00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:18.400
You do.
确实如此。

73
00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.800
Wait, I need a picture of you doing that.
等等，我需要一张你做这个动作的照片。

74
00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.230
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

75
00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:25.930
All right.
好吧。

76
00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:26.970
Well, we're very excited.
总之，我们非常兴奋。

77
00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.430
Our book is coming out in two weeks.
我们的书两周后就要出版了。

78
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.370
We can't believe it.
我们简直不敢相信。

79
00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.950
I can't promise I'm going to wear a fakie flower, everyone.
各位，我不能保证我会戴假花。

80
00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:33.170
I'm sorry to disappoint.
很抱歉让大家失望了。

81
00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.130
I'm still trying.
我还在努力。

82
00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:35.670
You got to have one, Jenna.
你得戴一个，珍娜。

83
00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:36.290
Just one.
就戴一个。

84
00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.470
I'll work on it.
我会努力的。

85
00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:38.710
All right.
好吧。

86
00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.370
Let's get into fast facts.
让我们进入快速问答环节。

87
00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.370
Fast fact number one.
快速问答第一条。

88
00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:45.610
John Krasinski directed this episode.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基执导了这一集。

89
00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:46.730
My gosh.
天哪。

90
00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.410
We had a fan question from Alice R.
我们有一个来自意大利的

91
00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.010
in Italy.
粉丝爱丽丝·R的提问。

92
00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:50.810
No.
不会吧。

93
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:56.550
How was it seeing John Krasinski on the other side of the camera as director?
看到约翰·卡拉辛斯基作为导演站在摄像机背后是什么感觉？

94
00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.930
He did an amazing job.
他做得太棒了。

95
00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.090
He sure did.
他确实做得很好。

96
00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.610
He was just like a natural.
他简直天生就是干这个的。

97
00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.970
He really was.
他真的是。

98
00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.790
It was a total pleasure.
这绝对是一种享受。

99
00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.410
It was always tricky.
这总是很棘手。

100
00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:11.030
What was it going to be like when one of our castmates stepped into directing?
当我们的某位演员同事开始尝试导演时，会是什么样的情况？

101
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:14.970
Particularly because they had to be on both sides of the camera.
特别是考虑到他们必须兼顾镜头的两边。

102
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.070
Like, logistically, how does that work?
就后勤而言，这到底是怎么运作的？

103
00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:17.630
Right.
没错。

104
00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.590
And John was your major scene partner.
而且约翰是你主要的对手戏演员。

105
00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:20.310
He was.
他是。

106
00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:25.930
It was so crazy how we could do scenes together and he would be completely in character as Jim.
太疯狂了，我们一起拍戏时，他能完全沉浸在吉姆这个角色里。

107
00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:34.350
I felt like I was talking to Jim, but then we would cut and he would have simultaneously observed things and would have notes.
我觉得我当时就是在和吉姆说话，但一喊停，他又能同时注意到各种情况并给出意见。

108
00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:35.470
I don't know how he did.
我不知道他是怎么做到的。

109
00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:36.510
I don't know how your brain does that.
我不知道你的大脑是怎么做那类事的。

110
00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:37.190
My brain doesn't do that.
我的大脑可做不到。

111
00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.590
Some people have that brain, though.
不过有些人确实有那种大脑。

112
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.990
They just compartmentalize it and then they know how to, like, I'm sort of a one-trick pony.
他们只是把它分门别类，然后就知道怎么去……我这个人有点只会一招。

113
00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:43.910
I know.
我懂。

114
00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:45.850
I like to be doing the one thing artistically.
我喜欢在艺术上专心做好一件事。

115
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.230
The one thing.
就那一件事。

116
00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.170
I'm real good at the one thing at one time.
我擅长在同一时间专心做好一件事。

117
00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:56.810
Well, we reached out to John and he's off right now filming season three of Jack Ryan, but he sent in some audio clips.
我们联系了约翰，他现在正在外地拍摄《杰克·莱恩》第三季，不过他发来了一些音频片段。

118
00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:58.950
And we're so excited to share them with you.
我们非常高兴能与大家分享。

119
00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:02.710
First off, he talked about what it was like to direct the show.
首先，他谈到了执导这部剧的感受。

120
00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.630
Hi, guys.
嗨，大家好。

121
00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:05.770
Wait a minute.
等一下。

122
00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.690
How are you on Saber already?
你们怎么已经讲到《沙巴》那集了？

123
00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.450
That means that it is season six?
那意味着已经第六季了吗？

124
00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:13.210
You're into season six?
你们都讲到第六季了？

125
00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:13.710
No.
不。

126
00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.230
Slow down.
慢点。

127
00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:17.110
We need more of this podcaSt.
我们需要更多的播客内容。

128
00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.330
The world needs more of this podcast for the love of Pete.
为了老天爷好，这个世界需要更多的播客内容。

129
00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:22.170
That's all I have to say about that.
关于这个，我就想说这么多。

130
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:23.990
What was it like directing Saber?
执导《沙巴》是什么感觉？

131
00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.910
It was a dream.
那简直是个梦想。

132
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:30.850
It was absolutely everything you would wish directing a show like this would be.
绝对符合你对执导这样一部剧的所有美好期望。

133
00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:35.910
I personally was terrified because I had to direct all of you.
我个人当时吓坏了，因为我得导演你们所有人。

134
00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:41.630
I remember being really, really nervous about that, that you were my coworkers, but you were my closest friends.
我记得对此感到非常非常紧张，因为你们既是我的同事，也是我最亲密的朋友。

135
00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.590
You were my family.
你们是我的家人。

136
00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:50.290
And here I was thinking I had the audacity to tell you what to do, which incidentally, I don't think I did once.
而我当时竟然觉得自己有脸告诉你们该怎么做，顺便说一句，我觉得我一次也没这么做过。

137
00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:55.850
I'm not sure I gave one acting note to any of you because I was just in awe watching, sitting back and watching.
我甚至不确定自己有没有给你们任何一个人提过表演方面的建议，因为我坐在后面看着，只有惊叹的份。

138
00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:05.370
Which really was one of the most special parts about directing the show was getting to see through a totally unique lens of being behind these monitors.
这也确实是执导这部剧最特别的地方之一，那就是通过一种完全独特的视角——坐在这些监视器后面去观察。

139
00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:17.270
The magic that every single one of you brought to each and every moment, whether it was a joke or whether it was an emotional beat, everyone was just so good at what they did.
你们每个人在每一个时刻所展现出的魔力，无论是一个笑话还是一个情感节点，每个人都把自己的工作做得太出色了。

140
00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.610
And of course, as an actor, I always used to love watching everybody play in these scenes.
当然，作为一个演员，我以前总是喜欢看大家在这些场景里飙戏。

141
00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.250
But there were so many scenes that I wasn't a part of.
但有许多场景我是没有参与的。

142
00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:32.890
So, you know, getting to in Saber, getting to be a part of the hot tub scene with Michael and David Wallace.
所以，你知道，在《沙巴》里，能参与迈克尔和大卫·华莱士的热水浴缸戏。

143
00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:43.390
At the end of the day, I think that directing that episode was a much bigger deal than I even understood or imagined then in that moment.
说实话，我觉得导演那一集比我当时所理解或想象的要重大得多。

144
00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.550
Because the truth is, directing is terrifying.
因为事实是，导演工作令人胆战心惊。

145
00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:51.530
As I told you, I was very nervous to do it on this show.
正如我所告诉你们的，在这部剧里尝试这个，我当时非常紧张。

146
00:06:51.850 --> 00:07:03.270
And honestly, if it hadn't been for this episode being such an amazing experience, surrounded by such hugely supportive crew members, cast members, producers, everyone,
老实说，如果不是因为这一集是一次如此美妙的经历，周围又有如此全力支持我们的剧组人员、演员、制片人以及所有人，

147
00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.910
I don't know that I ever would have done it again.
我不知道自己以后是否还会再做导演。

148
00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:06.810
Truly.
真的。

149
00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:15.910
I mean, I think it was something that I was really excited to experiment with on our show, but never thought that I'd go much further than that in trying to direct anything else.
我的意思是，我觉得当时只是很兴奋能在我们的剧里尝试这个，但从未想过要在尝试导演其他作品时走得更远。

150
00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:17.770
Can you imagine?
你能想象吗？

151
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.190
Oh, man.
天哪。

152
00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.430
Could you imagine if he didn't keep directing?
你能想象如果他没有继续当导演会怎样吗？

153
00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:22.450
He's so good.
他太优秀了。

154
00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:23.150
I know.
我懂。

155
00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:31.190
I just love that John got to have this experience on our show for the first time because you and I know how loving and supportive everyone was.
我真的很开心约翰能在我们的剧组里第一次拥有这样的经历，因为你我都清楚每个人是多么有爱和支持。

156
00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:33.770
This was true for other people as well.
对其他人来说也是如此。

157
00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:39.150
I mean, our editor, Claire Scanlon, has a very successful directing career in television.
我是说，我们的剪辑师克莱尔·斯坎伦在电视界有着非常成功的导演生涯。

158
00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.690
That started with The Office.
那是从《办公室》开始的。

159
00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:52.690
That was because Greg was very encouraging of having different department heads step into that role of director to step out of what they were doing and try this new thing in a really supportive environment.
那是因为格雷格非常鼓励各个部门的负责人去尝试导演的角色，走出他们原本的岗位，在一个充满支持的环境中尝试这件新事物。

160
00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:56.050
I feel like it launched the directing careers of many people.
我觉得这开启了许多人的导演生涯。

161
00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:58.730
Randall Einhorn, our cinematographer.
兰德尔·埃因霍ーン，我们的摄影师。

162
00:07:58.890 --> 00:07:59.510
Matt Sohn.
马特·索恩。

163
00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:00.070
Yes.
没错。

164
00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:00.610
So many.
太多人了。

165
00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:04.210
And, by the way, the writer of this episode, Jen Salata.
而且，顺便说一句，本集的编剧是珍·萨拉塔。

166
00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:04.530
Yeah.
对。

167
00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:06.650
I was just watching television the other day.
我前几天刚好看电视。

168
00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.290
I was watching Abbott Elementary, and she directed the episode.
我在看《小学风云》，那集就是她导演的。

169
00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.710
I was like, oh, my gosh.
我当时就想，天哪。

170
00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:10.930
Yeah.
对。

171
00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:11.390
Jen.
珍。

172
00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:12.750
So many people.
太多人了。

173
00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:13.630
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

174
00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:21.690
Speaking of Jen Salata, there is a great interview with her and John over on officetelly.com for this episode.
说到珍·萨拉塔，officetelly.com 上有一篇关于她和约翰针对本集的精彩采访。

175
00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:31.090
I'll share some of what they talked about as we go along, but one of the things that it included were interviews with cast members about John's directing.
随着节目的进行，我会分享一些他们谈论的内容，其中之一就包括对演员们关于约翰导演工作的采访。

176
00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.110
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

177
00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:32.630
Yes.
是的。

178
00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:34.150
So I'm going to tell you what people said.
所以我要告诉你们大家是怎么说的。

179
00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:34.490
All right.
好的。

180
00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:35.870
Ellie said,
艾莉说，

181
00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:41.690
John made me feel confident yet calm and also made me laugh throughout the entire week.
约翰让我感到自信而又冷静，而且在整个星期的拍摄过程中一直逗我笑。

182
00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:45.590
If it isn't too weird a thing to say, I feel like he took very good care of us.
如果这样说不算太奇怪的话，我觉得他把我们照顾得非常好。

183
00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.010
Oh.
哦。

184
00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.590
Brian said he was bold, which I thought was cool.
布莱恩说他很大胆，我觉得这很酷。

185
00:08:50.790 --> 00:08:52.730
He wanted characters to try new things.
他希望角色们尝试新事物。

186
00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:54.910
Kate said,
凯特说，

187
00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:59.030
John was a very thoughtful director who created a great tone on set.
约翰是一位非常细心的导演，他在片场营造了极佳的氛围。

188
00:08:59.070 --> 00:09:01.370
He really did his homework on all levels.
他在各个层面都做足了功课。

189
00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:04.170
He took his job very seriously, but not himself.
他非常认真对待自己的工作，但并不把自己当回事。

190
00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.110
Like, he didn't take himself too seriously.
比如说，他没有把自己看得太重要。

191
00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.050
That's John.
这很约翰。

192
00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:08.470
And then Creed said,
然后克里德说，

193
00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:09.870
Which one's John?
哪个是约翰？

194
00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.290
Oh, my gosh, Creed.
哦，天哪，克里德。

195
00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.890
Creed with the button.
克里德真是神来之笔。

196
00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:13.970
So perfect.
太完美了。

197
00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:15.190
All right.
好的。

198
00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:21.210
Fast fact number two, I'll have you know, this was not John's directorial debut.
冷知识第二条，我要告诉你们，这并不是约翰的导演处女作。

199
00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:22.470
What was?
那什么是？

200
00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.410
So this might have been the thing that inspired him to keep directing, but it was not his debut.
所以这可能是启发他继续当导演的原因，但它并不是他的处女作。

201
00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:31.610
He had written, produced, and directed the film Brief Interviews with Hideous Men,
他曾亲自编剧、制片并导演了电影《简短访谈与丑陋男子》，

202
00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.290
based on the short story collection by David Foster Wallace.
该片改编自大卫·福斯特·华莱士的短篇小说集。

203
00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:36.990
I remember this.
我记得这个。

204
00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:41.190
From the time we did the pilot, John loved this book.
从我们拍试播集开始，约翰就非常喜欢这本书。

205
00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:48.070
And I guess he purchased the rights to the book with his first paycheck from the office.
我猜他是用拍《办公室》赚到的第一笔片酬买下了这本书的版权。

206
00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.870
He had always wanted to adapt it.
他一直都想把它改编成电影。

207
00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.250
He's so smart like that.
他在这方面真的很聪明。

208
00:09:51.390 --> 00:09:51.970
I know.
我知道。

209
00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.530
He's such a forward thinker.
他是个很有远见的人。

210
00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:54.170
He is.
确实如此。

211
00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.070
Originally, he was just going to write and produce the film.
起初，他只打算写剧本并担任制片人。

212
00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:00.970
Did you know John majored in screenwriting at Brown University?
你知道约翰在布朗大学主修的是编剧专业吗？

213
00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:02.270
I didn't know that.
我不知道这件事。

214
00:10:02.570 --> 00:10:02.630
No.
不知道。

215
00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:03.170
Yeah.
是的。

216
00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.270
So he majored in screenwriting, not acting.
所以他主修的是编剧，而不是表演。

217
00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.290
Writing was really his first love.
写作其实才是他的初恋。

218
00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:12.090
So anyway, he had the rights, but he couldn't find a director.
总之，他有了版权，却找不到合适的导演。

219
00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:17.190
And I guess it was Rainn Wilson who said to him on set one day,
我猜有一天在片场是雷恩·威尔逊对他说，

220
00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.170
why don't you just direct it yourself?
你怎么不自己当导演呢？

221
00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:20.890
That sounds like Rainn, too.
这也太像雷恩会说的话了。

222
00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:21.130
Yeah.
就是。

223
00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:21.350
Right.
没错。

224
00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:24.090
Rainn is very much the person that's like, why don't you just do it?
雷恩就是那种总是对你说“你怎么不自己干”的人。

225
00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.590
And you're like, oh, well, okay.
然后你就会觉得，哦，好吧。

226
00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:26.530
Yeah.
对。

227
00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:32.250
So I guess Rainn Wilson kind of kickstarted John's directing career.
所以我觉得雷恩·威尔逊算是开启了约翰的导演生涯。

228
00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.450
The next thing he directed was this episode of The Office.
他接下来导演的作品就是《办公室》的这一集。

229
00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.510
Then he directed two more episodes of The Office.
之后他又执导了两集《办公室》。

230
00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.470
So three total.
总共就是三集。

231
00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:43.230
Then when The Office was over, he directed a movie called The Hollers.
后来《办公室》剧终时，他导演了一部名为《霍勒家的权色交易》的电影。

232
00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:45.770
And of course, A Quiet Place.
当然还有《寂静之地》。

233
00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.950
Which I watched on the plane.
我是在飞机上看的。

234
00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:48.810
Oh, lady.
天呐，老姐。

235
00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:49.410
Was I crazy?
我当时是不是疯了？

236
00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:50.270
Oh, lady.
天呐。

237
00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:51.990
Did you yell out?
你当时叫出声了吗？

238
00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:52.650
Yes.
叫了。

239
00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:55.970
I was like, I'm sure people thought I was crazy.
我当时就想，其他人肯定觉得我疯了。

240
00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.190
Oh, my gosh.
我的天啊。

241
00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:02.270
Well, you know, his next directorial project is a film called If,
对了，他下一个导演项目是一部叫《神秘友友》的电影，

242
00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.530
and he's reuniting with Steve Carell.
而且他将和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔再度合作。

243
00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.630
Steve's going to be in it.
史蒂夫会出演这部电影。

244
00:11:05.750 --> 00:11:06.530
Oh, my gosh.
我的天呐。

245
00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:07.690
We have to go see that together.
我们一定要一起去看。

246
00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:08.790
Let's do it.
一言为定。

247
00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:12.950
So one more thing I want to point out before we move on to Fast Fact No.
所以在我们进入第三号冷知识之前，我还有一件事要指出，

248
00:11:12.990 --> 00:11:13.130
3,
3,

249
00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.070
because Fast Fact No.
因为第三号冷知识

250
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:15.070
3 is all Angela.
全都是关于安吉拉的。

251
00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:15.870
Oh, no.
哦，不。

252
00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.710
So I'm squeezing a little extra information into my Fast Fact 2.
所以我把一点额外的 信息塞进了我的“快速事实2”里。

253
00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:20.410
Squeeze it.
塞吧。

254
00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:26.250
Which is that we need to point out what a very big deal it was for John to direct this particular
那就是我们需要指出，约翰来执导这一集 是件多么了不起的事，

255
00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:31.890
episode, because he had to establish two new major characters in the show.
因为他必须在剧中塑造两个全新的重要角色。

256
00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:36.830
Kathy Bates as Joe Bennett and Zach Woods as Gabe Lewis.
饰演乔·贝内特的凯西·贝茨和饰演盖布·刘易斯的扎克·伍兹。

257
00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.610
And he directed Christian Slater.
而且他还执导了克里斯蒂安·史莱特。

258
00:11:39.850 --> 00:11:42.990
So this was not just a regular episode of The Office.
所以这可不仅仅是《办公室》里普通的一集。

259
00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:44.850
He had to do the whole Sabre video.
他还得搞定整个赛博公司的视频。

260
00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.450
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

261
00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:46.310
I didn't even think about that.
我甚至都没想到这一点。

262
00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:47.710
He had to start a whole new company.
他得创立一个全新的公司。

263
00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:50.270
He had to, like, establish Sabre.
他不得不，比如说，建立赛博公司。

264
00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.230
Well, it's a big episode to make your directorial debut, my lord.
天哪，作为导演处女作来说，这一集可真够分量的。

265
00:11:54.470 --> 00:11:56.770
Well, John talked a little bit about it.
嗯，约翰稍微聊了聊这事。

266
00:11:57.030 --> 00:11:57.570
Here we go.
我们听听。

267
00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:01.510
Introducing Kathy Bates, which was so mind-blowing.
介绍凯西·贝茨登场，这太让人震撼了。

268
00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:07.030
The Kathy Bates was not only on our show, but I was her first experience as a director.
凯西·贝茨不仅来到了我们的剧组，而且我还是她作为导演的第一个经历。

269
00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:10.070
And for that, I will always be apologetic to her.
为此，我将永远对她感到抱歉。

270
00:12:10.070 --> 00:12:14.850
But I remember introducing that character and knowing that, I don't know, feeling a big
但我记得在引出那个角色时，我有一种，怎么说呢，感到责任重大，

271
00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:17.950
responsibility, that that character was going to be a big part of the show.
因为那个角色将成为剧中的重要部分。

272
00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:24.230
And bringing along with her was Zach Woods, who I remember from the moment we shot his
随她一同登场的是扎克·伍兹，我还记得从我们拍摄他第一场戏的那一刻起，也就是整段矿泉水瓶的剧情，

273
00:12:24.230 --> 00:12:28.150
first stuff, the whole water bottle storyline.
他简直搞笑得难以置信。

274
00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.430
He was just so unbelievably funny.
他在剧中需要用到这个全新的喜剧工具时显得那么内敛，这是一个与其他人完全不同的角色。

275
00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:36.770
He was so reserved in this brand new instrument that we had to play with on the show, a totally
然而，每当他开口说话，你的视线就无法从他身上移开。

276
00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:38.390
different character than anybody else.
他一直都非常、非常搞笑。

277
00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:42.850
And yet, whenever he spoke, you couldn't take your eyes off of him.
我只记得随着剧中重大剧情的转变发生，

278
00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.850
He was always so, so funny.
我作为引出这两个角色的人感到非常紧张。

279
00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.530
And I just remember with the big story changes that were happening in the show, I was so
但到头来，怎么说呢，能成为其中的一部分让我感到有些荣幸。

280
00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.770
nervous to be the one to introduce those two characters.
我觉得这些人能让约翰当导演真是走运。

281
00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:57.470
And then in the end, I don't know, feel somewhat honored to have been a part of it.
他太有亲和力了。

282
00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:00.690
I think those guys were lucky to have John as a director.
他能让你感到非常轻松。

283
00:13:00.930 --> 00:13:02.270
He's so personable.
我是说，听着，我们所有的导演在我心中都有一席之地。

284
00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:03.730
He puts you so at ease.
他们都很棒。

285
00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:07.790
I mean, listen, all of our directors have a place in my heart.
但约翰确实有一种天赋，能走进一个房间，让每个人都放松下来。

286
00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:08.570
They're all great.
你知道我的意思吗？

287
00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:15.570
But John really does have a gift at walking into a room and just putting everyone out of
他很擅长建立连接。

288
00:13:15.570 --> 00:13:16.090
their heads.
的确如此。

289
00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:16.910
Do you know what I mean?
他很擅长瞬间建立连接。

290
00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:17.990
He's a good connector.
好了，安吉拉。

291
00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:18.390
He is.
轮到你了。

292
00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:19.990
He's good at connecting instantly.
这是“快速事实3”。

293
00:13:21.130 --> 00:13:21.750
All right, Angela.
你给我准备了什么？

294
00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.090
It's you.
好的，给你。

295
00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.390
It's Fast Fact 3.
“快速事实”第3条由乔亚·巴尔弗提供。

296
00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:25.450
What do you got for me?
哦！

297
00:13:25.530 --> 00:13:26.750
Okay, here you go.
如你们所知，她曾在NBC数字部门工作。

298
00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.830
Fast Fact number 3 is courtesy of Joya Balfour.
嗯。

299
00:13:31.110 --> 00:13:31.450
Oh!
没错。

300
00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.110
Who, as you guys know, worked for NBC Digital.
对的。

301
00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:39.150
She shared with us that NBC did an entire website for Sabre.
她跟我们分享说，NBC为赛博公司做了一个完整的网站。

302
00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:46.830
The site featured a bio on CEO Joe Bennett, the full Christian Slater video, a section with
网站上有关于首席执行官乔·贝内特的简介、完整的克里斯蒂安·史莱特视频、一个包含

303
00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:50.430
a company overview, plus it featured all of Sabre's...
公司概况的板块，此外还收录了赛博所有的……

304
00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.110
Sabre, oh my God, I'm doing it.
赛博，天哪，我又说错名字了。

305
