Say Dunder Miffin and Saber.
说邓德·米弗林和雪芭。

750
00:32:55.580 --> 00:32:57.980
So yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
所以，耶，耶，耶，耶。

751
00:32:58.220 --> 00:33:00.320
Dunder Miffin is a part of Saber.
丹德·米夫林是赛博公司的一部分。

752
00:33:00.940 --> 00:33:03.480
Say yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
唱吧，耶，耶，耶，耶。

753
00:33:03.720 --> 00:33:06.100
Dunder Miffin is a part of Saber.
丹德·米夫林是赛博公司的一部分。

754
00:33:06.440 --> 00:33:07.660
Dunder Miffin is a part of Saber.
丹德·米夫林是赛博公司的一部分。

755
00:33:08.460 --> 00:33:09.220
Oh my God.
我的天哪。

756
00:33:09.400 --> 00:33:10.580
It makes me laugh so hard.
这让我笑得停不下来。

757
00:33:11.460 --> 00:33:12.900
They're really good, too.
而且它们真的很棒。

758
00:33:12.900 --> 00:33:14.120
I know they are.
我知道它们很棒。

759
00:33:14.360 --> 00:33:16.600
We had a fan question from Rachel S.
我们收到了来自阿肯色州本顿市的瑞秋·S的粉丝提问，

760
00:33:16.800 --> 00:33:21.580
in Benton, Arkansas, who wrote the Saber song to the tune
她把赛博之歌填到了

761
00:33:21.580 --> 00:33:22.560
Party in the USA.
《美国派对》的曲调里。

762
00:33:23.060 --> 00:33:28.280
Rachel, it was scripted by our writers Warren Lieberstein and Halstead Sullivan.
瑞秋，这是由我们的编剧沃伦·利伯斯坦和霍尔斯特德·沙利文写剧本的。

763
00:33:28.440 --> 00:33:30.840
Remember, those are the guys who wrote Koi Pond.
记住，就是写了《锦鲤池》的那两个家伙。

764
00:33:30.840 --> 00:33:40.460
Now, Jen Salata shared that they also had to write lyrics to two other songs because they didn't know what song was eventually going to get cleared.
现在，珍·萨拉塔分享说，他们当时还得为另外两首歌写歌词，因为他们不知道最后哪首歌能获得版权许可。

765
00:33:40.460 --> 00:33:48.340
So I guess they wrote lyrics to I Got a Feelin' by Black Eyed Peas and Surfin' in the USA by the Beach Boys.
所以我猜他们为黑眼豆豆的《我有一种感觉》和海滩男孩的《美国冲浪》写了歌词。

766
00:33:48.340 --> 00:33:52.920
But they did eventually get the rights to Party in the USA.
但他们最终还是拿到了《美国派对》的版权。

767
00:33:52.920 --> 00:33:57.760
It's something called Song Parody Rights, and it costs $23,000.
这叫做歌曲恶搞版权，花了两万三千美元。

768
00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:03.900
Well, I texted Warren about this, and I was like, how did you guys get assigned to writing this?
嗯，我为此给沃伦发了短信，我说，你们是怎么被指派写这个的？

769
00:34:04.040 --> 00:34:09.500
And he said, Halstead and I both sang acapella in college, and we were a little nerdy about it.
他说，我和霍尔斯特德上大学时都唱过阿卡贝拉，我们对此有点书呆子气。

770
00:34:09.660 --> 00:34:13.080
This was before Pitch Perfect made acapella nerdy cool.
这是在《完美音调》让阿卡贝拉变得像书呆子一样酷之前的事。

771
00:34:14.680 --> 00:34:16.940
So the writers kind of knew us as that.
