我们没有机会见到克里斯蒂安·史莱特。

922
00:41:56.050 --> 00:41:57.350
We didn't get to work with him.
我们没能跟他合作。

923
00:41:57.390 --> 00:41:58.290
We were so bummed.
我们太沮丧了。

924
00:41:58.370 --> 00:41:59.730
We were majorly bummed.
我们心里别提多失落了。

925
00:41:59.790 --> 00:42:02.290
Because everyone was talking about what a nice guy he was.
因为每个人都在说他是个多么好的人。

926
00:42:02.570 --> 00:42:05.390
Well, we got a fan question from Natasha in Wales.
好吧，我们收到了来自威尔士的娜塔莎的一个粉丝提问。

927
00:42:05.770 --> 00:42:08.630
Where was the Christian Slater sequence shot?
克里斯蒂安·史莱特的那些镜头是在哪里拍的？

928
00:42:08.630 --> 00:42:09.890
Was it close by?
离得近吗？

929
00:42:10.290 --> 00:42:13.410
I got a location breakdown from Randy Cordray.
我拿到了兰迪·科德雷给的场地明细。

930
00:42:13.610 --> 00:42:14.090
Do it.
快说吧。

931
00:42:14.490 --> 00:42:21.250
The interior shots, including the cafeteria, which, by the way, I asked Randy, was that the IKEA cafeteria?
内景部分，包括食堂——顺便说一句，我问过兰迪，那是宜家的食堂吗？

932
00:42:21.250 --> 00:42:23.550
It really looks like my IKEA cafeteria.
看起来真的很像我去的宜家食堂。

933
00:42:23.850 --> 00:42:24.590
It really does.
真的超级像。

934
00:42:24.590 --> 00:42:25.710
We go to the same one.
我们去的是同一家。

935
00:42:25.810 --> 00:42:26.950
I was like, where are the meatballs?
我当时就在想，肉丸在哪呢？

936
00:42:27.170 --> 00:42:28.450
That looks like the cafeteria.
那看起来太像食堂了。

937
00:42:28.450 --> 00:42:29.510
He said no.
他说不是。

938
00:42:29.690 --> 00:42:34.510
They were filmed at the Lakeview Corporate Center in Westlake Village, California.
它们是在加利福尼亚州韦斯特莱克村的湖景企业中心拍摄的。

939
00:42:35.070 --> 00:42:40.450
Randy said that they were mostly unoccupied at the time, so we were able to dress them to look like whatever we needed.
兰迪说当时那里大部分都是空置的，所以我们可以根据需要把它们布置成任何想要的样子。

940
00:42:40.450 --> 00:42:41.650
We made that cafeteria.
那个食堂是我们自己搭出来的。

941
00:42:42.030 --> 00:42:45.990
The exterior shots were shot at the Baxter Building.
外景是在巴克斯特大楼拍的。

942
00:42:46.470 --> 00:42:52.990
Randy complimented our locations manager, Kyle Alexander, because he was able to find these two spots right next to one another.
兰迪夸奖了我们的外景经理凯尔·亚历山大，因为他找到了这两个紧挨着的地方。

943
00:42:52.990 --> 00:43:05.010
It made it really easy to shoot those sequences in one day, and John shared that when they got to the location, that exterior location, there was a pond in front of the building,
这使得在一天内拍完那些镜头变得非常容易，约翰分享说，当他们到达那个外景地点时，建筑物前面有一个池塘，

944
00:43:05.010 --> 00:43:11.150
and it had a bunch of ducks in it, like 30 ducks, and John was super excited.
里面有一群鸭子，大概有30只，约翰超级兴奋。

945
00:43:11.390 --> 00:43:19.210
He absolutely loved this detail, so he put Christian Slater's opening shot right in front of the pond with the ducks.
他极其喜欢这个细节，所以他把克里斯蒂安·史莱特的开场镜头直接安排在有鸭子的池塘前面。

946
00:43:19.210 --> 00:43:30.630
But right before they were about to shoot, one of the location guys got into the pond because they were trying to get the ducks to come just a little bit closer.
但就在他们准备开拍之前，其中一个现场工作人员走进了池塘，因为他们想让鸭子离镜头再近一点点。

947
00:43:30.870 --> 00:43:31.590
To camera?
靠近镜头？

948
00:43:31.810 --> 00:43:32.110
Yes.
对。

949
00:43:32.510 --> 00:43:33.530
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

950
00:43:33.990 --> 00:43:35.590
All the ducks flew away.
所有的鸭子都飞走了。

951
00:43:35.770 --> 00:43:37.570
They were like, get out of our pond, mister.
他们就像是说：‘从我们的池塘里滚出去，先生。’

952
00:43:38.310 --> 00:43:39.490
John was so bummed.
约翰当时沮丧极了。

953
00:43:40.050 --> 00:43:47.930
And then our writer, Jen Salata, shared that Greg Daniels pitched that line, have you ever tasted a rainbow?
然后我们的编剧珍·萨拉塔分享说，格雷格·丹尼尔斯提出了那句台词：‘你尝过彩虹的味道吗？’

954
00:43:47.930 --> 00:43:49.630
Oh my gosh, so brilliant.
哦，天哪，太绝了。

955
00:43:49.670 --> 00:43:50.530
That was from Greg.
那是格雷格想出来的。

956
00:43:50.930 --> 00:43:53.590
It was even used in the promo that you played.
甚至在你播放的宣传片里也用了这句。

957
00:43:54.050 --> 00:43:58.010
They did have some alts, like, have you ever tasted a smile?
他们其实还有一些备选，比如：‘你尝过微笑的味道吗？’

958
00:43:58.270 --> 00:44:00.930
But ultimately, they kept the rainbow line.
但最终，他们保留了彩虹那句。

959
00:44:01.190 --> 00:44:06.210
They also experimented with different things that Christian Slater could be doing on that line.
他们还尝试了克里斯蒂安·史莱特在说那句台词时可以做的不同动作。

960
00:44:06.450 --> 00:44:11.150
Like, at one point, I guess they had him carrying around a giant basket of fruit.
比如，有一个阶段，我猜他们让他扛着一大篮水果。

961
00:44:12.110 --> 00:44:15.050
But they loved him picking up the sandwich.
但他们更喜欢他捡起三明治的样子。

962
00:44:15.410 --> 00:44:15.650
Yeah.
对。

963
00:44:15.650 --> 00:44:18.770
I mean, they must have had so much fun shooting.
我的意思是，他们拍摄时一定玩得超开心。

964
00:44:18.890 --> 00:44:21.110
They were just doing these weird, absurd things.
他们就是在做这些古怪、荒谬的事情。

965
00:44:21.330 --> 00:44:23.730
And Christian was playing it so straight the whole time.
而克里斯蒂安全程都演得非常一本正经。

966
00:44:23.730 --> 00:44:24.310
It's amazing.
这太厉害了。

967
00:44:24.870 --> 00:44:33.390
Well, in the Entertainment Weekly article he did, the interviewer asked him if he ad-libbed anything, commenting that the thumbs up at the end was classic.
嗯，在他为《娱乐周刊》拍摄的那篇报道中，采访者问他有没有即兴发挥，并评论说最后的竖大拇指简直是经典。

968
00:44:33.690 --> 00:44:33.910
Oh.
哦。

969
00:44:34.310 --> 00:44:35.710
Here was Christian's response.
以下是克里斯蒂安的回答。

970
00:44:36.070 --> 00:44:38.410
The thumbs up was a spontaneous moment.
竖大拇指是一个即兴的时刻。

971
00:44:38.410 --> 00:44:42.130
I just kind of thought, what would be the cheesiest thing to do?
我当时就想，做什么动作会是最俗气的？

972
00:44:42.810 --> 00:44:49.830
John wanted it to really look like Kathy Bates paid for this actor to come in and directed him on what to do behind the scenes.
约翰希望看起来真的像是凯西·贝茨花钱请这个演员来，并在幕后指导他该怎么做。

973
00:44:49.990 --> 00:44:53.550
So I just kept thinking, what would Kathy Bates tell me to do?
所以我一直在想，凯西·贝茨会让我做什么？

974
00:44:53.550 --> 00:44:55.710
I love that motivation.
我太喜欢这个动机了。

975
00:44:56.250 --> 00:44:57.910
Of course, Kathy Bates as Joe Bennett.
当然，凯西·贝茨饰演的是乔·贝内特。

976
00:44:58.070 --> 00:44:58.610
As Joe Bennett.
也就是乔·贝内特。

977
00:44:58.810 --> 00:44:59.090
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

978
00:44:59.510 --> 00:45:02.810
Well, we had a fan question from Fiona L.
我们收到了来自澳大利亚墨尔本的Fiona L.的粉丝提问。

979
00:45:02.990 --> 00:45:04.250
in Melbourne, Australia.
在墨尔本，澳大利亚。

980
00:45:04.570 --> 00:45:07.370
Our fan questions are very international today.
我们今天的粉丝提问非常具有国际化呢。

981
00:45:07.730 --> 00:45:16.090
Well, actually, Fiona has something to tell us, which is that Christian Slater does ads very similar to the Saber introduction video.
好吧，其实菲奥娜有个发现要告诉我们，那就是克里斯蒂安·史莱特拍的广告和塞伯公司介绍视频非常相似。

982
00:45:16.250 --> 00:45:19.330
They are for HP Wolf Security.
那是为惠普狼式安全（HP Wolf Security）拍的。

983
00:45:19.630 --> 00:45:24.910
They seem very tongue-in-cheek, especially because he's done this Saber video.
它们看起来非常带有反讽色彩，特别是考虑到他拍过那个塞伯视频之后。

984
00:45:25.170 --> 00:45:26.710
I have never seen this commercial.
我从来没看过这个广告。

985
00:45:27.010 --> 00:45:34.290
I want to say thank you, Fiona, for sending me down the rabbit hole that is the Wolf HP web series.
我要感谢菲奥娜，把我带进了惠普“恶狼”网络剧集的无底洞里。

986
00:45:34.290 --> 00:45:40.310
It was a web series that they launched in 2017 starring Christian Slater.
那是他们在2017年推出的一部网络剧，由克里斯蒂安·史莱特主演。

987
00:45:40.490 --> 00:45:42.170
They're called The Wolf.
它们被称为《恶狼》。

988
00:45:42.610 --> 00:45:47.450
And I think Christian Slater is the Wolf because he howls in it.
而且我认为克里斯蒂安·史莱特就是那只狼，因为他在里面会狼嚎。

989
00:45:47.550 --> 00:45:47.830
What?
什么？

990
00:45:48.030 --> 00:45:48.610
He howls.
他会狼嚎。

991
00:45:48.790 --> 00:45:53.430
He walks through companies, kind of like he does in the Saber video.
他走过各个公司，有点像他在塞伯视频里做的那样。

992
00:45:53.590 --> 00:45:56.530
You know, like he walks through the conference room while a meeting is happening.
你知道的，就像开会时他从会议室走过一样。

993
00:45:56.530 --> 00:46:05.450
And all the while he is highlighting how easily it would be for him to hack in to this company's printer or their computer.
与此同时，他一直在强调他黑进这家公司的打印机或电脑是多么轻而易举。

994
00:46:05.770 --> 00:46:08.530
He sort of narrates as he's walking through.
他在边走边进行某种旁白。

995
00:46:08.610 --> 00:46:09.830
I pulled a clip.
我截取了一段音频。

996
00:46:11.110 --> 00:46:13.070
Sheep never realizes a wolf around.
绵羊永远不会意识到身边有狼。

997
00:46:15.780 --> 00:46:17.900
And they do exactly what the wolf expects them to do.
它们做着狼期望它们做的所有事情。

998
00:46:18.320 --> 00:46:19.780
They run into each other.
它们撞在一起。

999
00:46:19.960 --> 00:46:20.900
They fall down.
它们摔倒。

1000
00:46:21.540 --> 00:46:22.780
They become dinner.
它们成了盘中餐。

1001
00:46:25.490 --> 00:46:26.390
Time to eat.
该吃饭了。

1002
00:46:29.930 --> 00:46:33.950
They've got no idea I used my phone to hack the OS on that printer over there.
他们绝对想不到我用手机黑了那边那台打印机的操作系统。

1003
00:46:35.090 --> 00:46:36.090
And why would they?
他们怎么会想到呢？

1004
00:46:36.850 --> 00:46:40.190
Not one printer in this place has built-in malware protection.
这里连一台内置恶意软件防护的打印机都没有。

1005
00:46:40.770 --> 00:46:44.850
Now, while they're all busy watching a little something I threw up on the control panel...
现在，趁他们都在忙着看我在控制面板上搞出来的小把戏……

1006
00:46:45.430 --> 00:46:46.790
Just look at your screen.
看看你的屏幕。

1007
00:46:47.970 --> 00:46:51.770
I can intercept all their print jobs until I find the info I'm looking for.
我可以拦截他们所有的打印任务，直到找到我想要的信息。

1008
00:46:52.730 --> 00:46:55.650
Ooh, today's somebody's birthday.
哦，今天有人过生日。

1009
00:46:56.190 --> 00:46:56.410
Perfect.
太完美了。

1010
00:46:57.790 --> 00:46:59.510
Really good stuff is upstairs.
楼上有真正的好东西。

1011
00:46:59.930 --> 00:47:06.350
The kind of stuff that could destroy any future this grand financial institution could hope to have.
那种足以彻底摧毁这家宏大金融机构任何未来希望的东西。

1012
00:47:07.450 --> 00:47:07.970
Oh!
哦！

1013
00:47:11.030 --> 00:47:12.730
Do you hear all the sheep noises?
你听到那些羊叫声了吗？

1014
00:47:12.730 --> 00:47:13.510
I can't talk.
我没法说话了。

1015
00:47:14.230 --> 00:47:17.150
Because all those people, the workers, they're just sheep.
因为所有这些员工，他们就像是一群绵羊。

1016
00:47:17.410 --> 00:47:17.930
They're juSt...
他们就跟……

1017
00:47:17.930 --> 00:47:19.550
Oh my gosh.
我的天哪。

1018
00:47:19.750 --> 00:47:21.990
And he's wolfing, you know?
而且他在学狼叫，你知道吗？

1019
00:47:22.230 --> 00:47:23.310
And then he howls!
然后他还在嚎叫！

1020
00:47:25.970 --> 00:47:30.610
That is the most dramatic, over-the-top corporate commercial I think I've ever heard.
这绝对是我听过最戏剧化、最夸张的企业广告了。

1021
00:47:30.730 --> 00:47:32.490
Like, we only could hear it.
就像是，我们只能听到声音。

1022
00:47:32.590 --> 00:47:33.890
Sam and I are dying laughing.
我和萨姆都快笑死了。

1023
00:47:34.070 --> 00:47:35.150
Like, we don't have a visual.
就像是，我们没有画面。

1024
00:47:35.350 --> 00:47:36.850
Like, just like you guys listening.
就像你们听众一样。

1025
00:47:37.910 --> 00:47:39.090
Oh my gosh.
我的天哪。

1026
00:47:39.230 --> 00:47:39.470
Yeah.
对。

1027
00:47:39.790 --> 00:47:40.130
Yeah.
对。

1028
00:47:40.130 --> 00:47:43.550
I mean, you guys, each one is like a few minutes long.
我是说，各位，每一个都长达好几分钟呢。

1029
00:47:43.550 --> 00:47:44.710
It was a whole series.
这是一整套系列广告。

1030
00:47:45.090 --> 00:47:45.390
Oh my gosh.
我的天哪。

1031
00:47:45.470 --> 00:47:47.650
And I love, like, really dramatically when he's like,
我特别喜欢那种超级戏剧化的桥段，当他说的时候，

1032
00:47:47.750 --> 00:47:48.710
they have no idea.
他们根本不知道。

1033
00:47:48.710 --> 00:47:49.930
I just hacked in.
我刚刚黑进去了。

1034
00:47:50.010 --> 00:47:50.350
Yeah.
对。

1035
00:47:50.490 --> 00:47:51.250
To their phone.
通过他们的手机。

1036
00:47:51.250 --> 00:47:57.070
Well, listen, I didn't know that you could hack into a printer until I watched this video.
听着，我看了这个视频才知道原来打印机也能被黑。

1037
00:47:57.210 --> 00:47:58.450
That's what he's doing in this clip.
这就是他在这个片段里做的事。

1038
00:47:58.650 --> 00:47:59.830
He's hacking into a printer.
他在黑进一台打印机。

1039
00:48:00.130 --> 00:48:01.470
Anything can be hacked, guys.
伙计们，什么东西都能被黑。

1040
00:48:01.990 --> 00:48:03.210
I learned something.
我学到了一课。

1041
00:48:03.670 --> 00:48:06.290
And I guess they just re-upped this campaign.
我猜他们最近又重新推出了这个宣传活动。

1042
00:48:07.110 --> 00:48:08.530
So, look for it.
所以，大家留意一下。

1043
00:48:08.690 --> 00:48:14.490
Well, remember years ago when we found out that you could hack someone's camera in their computer?
话说回来，还记得多年前我们发现别人的电脑摄像头也能被黑吗？

1044
00:48:14.490 --> 00:48:17.910
And so, then we started putting Post-it notes over our cameras.
然后我们就开始在摄像头上贴便签纸。

1045
00:48:17.970 --> 00:48:18.810
Over our camera.
贴在我们的摄像头上。

1046
00:48:18.990 --> 00:48:19.210
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1047
00:48:19.550 --> 00:48:20.090
I know.
我知道。

1048
00:48:20.170 --> 00:48:21.370
Everyone, you should do that.
每个人都该这么做。

1049
00:48:21.490 --> 00:48:24.370
You should put a Post-it note over the little camera in your computer.
你们应该在电脑的小摄像头上贴一张便签纸。

1050
00:48:24.510 --> 00:48:24.690
Right.
对吧。

1051
00:48:24.690 --> 00:48:26.210
Or a piece of tape or what have you.
或者一块胶带，诸如此类的东西。

1052
00:48:26.230 --> 00:48:30.090
Yes, because we read that article where you can hack into it.
对，因为我们读过那篇关于黑客入侵的文章。

1053
00:48:30.310 --> 00:48:30.510
Yeah.
没错。

1054
00:48:30.510 --> 00:48:32.530
And then people just watch you.
然后人们就会看着你。

1055
00:48:32.830 --> 00:48:33.690
In your house.
在你家里。

1056
00:48:33.870 --> 00:48:34.450
How creepy.
太毛骨悚然了。

1057
00:48:34.930 --> 00:48:35.850
It's creepskies.
简直是毛骨悚然本尊。

1058
00:48:36.190 --> 00:48:37.190
Super creeper.
超级大变态。

1059
00:48:37.810 --> 00:48:38.190
All right.
好了。

1060
00:48:38.330 --> 00:48:39.970
So, back to the conference room.
那么，回到会议室。

1061
00:48:40.050 --> 00:48:40.430
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1062
00:48:40.910 --> 00:48:42.350
Gabe has shown the video.
盖布已经播放了视频。

1063
00:48:42.610 --> 00:48:44.210
People are digesting it.
大家正在消化内容。

1064
00:48:44.210 --> 00:48:47.970
Jim has a sarcastic talking head about it.
吉姆对此有一段讽刺的单人访谈。

1065
00:48:48.050 --> 00:48:50.370
With a great impression by John Krasinski.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基模仿得太棒了。

1066
00:48:50.650 --> 00:48:51.330
Very good.
非常棒。

1067
00:48:51.490 --> 00:48:53.050
Well, you know he's good at the impressions.
你知道他很擅长模仿。

1068
00:48:53.350 --> 00:48:53.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1069
00:48:53.970 --> 00:48:58.430
Well, now Gabe is going to explain that Sabre primarily sells printers.
好，现在盖布要解释说，赛博公司主要卖的是打印机。

1070
00:48:58.850 --> 00:49:05.390
So, he wants everybody to consider themselves printer salesmen who also sell paper.
所以，他希望每个人都把自己当成兼卖纸张的打印机销售员。

1071
00:49:05.750 --> 00:49:07.050
Michael doesn't like this.
迈克尔不喜欢这样。

1072
00:49:07.170 --> 00:49:08.390
He doesn't care for it.
他对此很不感冒。

1073
00:49:08.430 --> 00:49:10.090
It's about to get worse for Michael, though.
不过，对迈克尔来说更糟的事情还在后头。

1074
00:49:10.450 --> 00:49:13.410
Gabe then starts going over all the new company policies.
接着盖布开始宣读所有公司新政策。

1075
00:49:13.410 --> 00:49:18.470
At 6 minutes 58 seconds, Meredith yells, talk about vacation days.
在6分58秒时，梅雷迪思大喊，谈谈假期吧。

1076
00:49:18.910 --> 00:49:20.990
Such an odd heckle from Meredith.
梅雷迪思这个起哄真是莫名其妙。

1077
00:49:21.770 --> 00:49:27.350
This was a much longer scene where everyone shares about their vacation days.
这本来是一场更长的戏，每个人都分享了自己的假期。

1078
00:49:27.630 --> 00:49:29.030
And Jenna, it just cracked me up.
珍娜，这真是把我笑死。

1079
00:49:29.110 --> 00:49:30.330
I want to share a little bit with you.
我想跟你们分享一点。

1080
00:49:30.890 --> 00:49:33.330
Meredith says, I saved up days from last year.
梅雷迪思说，我把去年的天数攒了下来。

1081
00:49:33.330 --> 00:49:34.750
I want to go to Jamaica.
我想去牙买加。

1082
00:49:34.750 --> 00:49:40.010
And then she stands up, rolls her hips, and says, how Meredith got her groove back.
然后她站起来，扭动着胯部说，看梅雷迪思如何重拾激情。

1083
00:49:40.390 --> 00:49:40.710
Okay.
好的。

1084
00:49:41.030 --> 00:49:41.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1085
00:49:41.910 --> 00:49:45.690
Stanley has a talking head where he says, I need those vacation days.
斯坦利有一段单人访谈，他说，我需要那些假期。

1086
00:49:45.690 --> 00:49:46.670
I have two women.
我有两个女人。

1087
00:49:46.830 --> 00:49:49.730
One likes to ski and one likes the tropics.
一个喜欢滑雪，一个喜欢热带风情。

1088
00:49:49.890 --> 00:49:50.790
It's very difficult.
这太难办了。

1089
00:49:50.970 --> 00:49:53.810
But I am not complaining or asking to be judged.
但我不是在抱怨，也不是在求评判。

1090
00:49:53.810 --> 00:49:55.230
I just need some time off.
我只是需要放假。

1091
00:49:55.770 --> 00:49:56.130
Okay.
好吧。

1092
00:49:56.130 --> 00:50:04.630
And then Michael says, what if you've been saving up for days like a big trip in the future, like a 40-day family safari?
然后迈克尔说，如果你一直在攒天数为了将来的大旅行，比如40天的家庭野生动物园之旅呢？

1093
00:50:05.510 --> 00:50:06.390
Oh, Michael.
哦，迈克尔。

1094
00:50:06.630 --> 00:50:12.010
Gabe says, I'm sorry, but maybe you could look into a two-week safari for your family.
盖布说，我很抱歉，但也许你可以考虑给家人安排一个两周的野生动物园之旅。

1095
00:50:12.410 --> 00:50:16.610
And Michael says, you can't take 12 kids on a safari in only two weeks.
迈克尔说，只有两周根本没法带12个孩子去野生动物园。

1096
00:50:17.050 --> 00:50:19.830
And Stanley says, you can if they're imaginary.
斯坦利说，如果他们是虚构的就可以。

1097
00:50:20.310 --> 00:50:21.730
Oh, my God.
我的天哪。

1098
00:50:21.790 --> 00:50:29.030
And then Kelly explains she actually owes the company days because she tried out for American Idol and took time off.
然后凯莉解释说她其实还欠公司假期，因为她去参加《美国偶像》面试请了假。

1099
00:50:29.190 --> 00:50:33.170
She went to Atlanta, Boston, and Cincinnati, and she did not advance.
她去了亚特兰大、波士顿和辛辛那提，而且没有晋级。

1100
00:50:33.930 --> 00:50:34.950
These are amazing.
这些真的太棒了。

1101
00:50:34.950 --> 00:50:35.490
I know.
我知道。

1102
00:50:35.590 --> 00:50:37.610
But here is my favorite part.
但接下来是我的最爱。

1103
00:50:37.890 --> 00:50:42.270
This scene would have ended with a line from Creed, and I am so bummed it got cut.
这场戏原本会以克里德的一句台词结尾，被剪掉了我真的超沮丧。

1104
00:50:42.270 --> 00:50:50.510
But while they're talking about their vacation time and whether it will roll over or not for Saber, Meredith sees the IT guy, right?
但就在他们讨论假期以及对塞伯来说假期能不能结转的时候，梅雷迪思看到了IT男，对吧？

1105
00:50:50.750 --> 00:50:51.070
Yes.
没错。

1106
00:50:51.230 --> 00:50:54.250
And she says, hey, who the hell's going through our stuff?
她说，嘿，到底是谁在翻我们的东西？

1107
00:50:54.610 --> 00:50:57.590
And Creed says, oh, that's just Sam.
克里德说，哦，那是山姆。

1108
00:50:57.750 --> 00:50:58.530
He's with me.
他跟我一起的。

1109
00:50:59.390 --> 00:50:59.870
What?
什么？

1110
00:51:00.890 --> 00:51:04.770
And then Gabe goes, actually, that's Nick, your new IT guy.
然后盖布说，其实那是尼克，你们的新IT男。

1111
00:51:04.930 --> 00:51:06.770
And then the scene progresses as aired.
然后剧情就照播出的那样继续下去了。

1112
00:51:06.970 --> 00:51:09.470
But I just love that Creed thought he knew this guy.
但我就是喜欢克里德以为他认识这个人。

1113
00:51:09.630 --> 00:51:10.530
He's like, oh, that's Sam.
他说，哦，那是山姆。

1114
00:51:10.770 --> 00:51:11.590
He's with me.
他跟我一起的。

1115
00:51:11.590 --> 00:51:14.830
Well, here is something that a lot of people flagged.
好了，这里有很多观众指出的一个细节。

1116
00:51:14.950 --> 00:51:28.770
When we cut over to Nick, the new IT guy, many people noticed that it is the same person who was giving graphic design career advice to Pam at the job fair.
当我们切到尼克——也就是新IT男时，很多人发现，他就是当年在招聘会上给潘提供平面设计职业建议的那个人。

1117
00:51:29.030 --> 00:51:29.490
Yeah.
对。

1118
00:51:29.730 --> 00:51:35.470
I asked Randy about this, and he said, well, now, job fair was not on his watch.
我问过兰迪这件事，他说，好吧，招聘会可不是在他当班的时候拍的。

1119
00:51:35.470 --> 00:51:45.510
But he did remember that a lot of the writers really, really loved this actor, who, by the way, Nelson Franklin, who previously appeared in job fair.
但他确实记得很多编剧非常非常喜欢这个演员——顺便说一下，他叫纳尔逊·富兰克林，之前在招聘会里出现过。

1120
00:51:45.670 --> 00:51:47.770
And they just decided, we don't care.
然后他们就决定，管他的。

1121
00:51:47.770 --> 00:51:50.030
We're going to bring him back because this is now an arc.
我们要把他找回来，因为这现在成了一个系列剧情。

1122
00:51:50.210 --> 00:51:52.770
He's going to appear in four episodes as Nick.
他会作为尼克出演四集。

1123
00:51:53.350 --> 00:51:55.350
He's really an amazing comedic actor.
他真的是个非常棒的喜剧演员。

1124
00:51:55.350 --> 00:51:59.310
You've probably seen him on Black-ish, Veep, Arrested Development.
你可能在《黑人当道》、《副总统》、《发展受阻》里见过他。

1125
00:51:59.570 --> 00:52:02.950
And Angela, you know him because you guys were both on Black AF together.
而且安吉拉，你认识他，因为你们一起演过《黑人阔少爷》。

1126
00:52:03.150 --> 00:52:03.770
We were.
我们确实合作过。

1127
00:52:03.990 --> 00:52:06.530
It was just the craziest little office reunion.
这简直是办公室里最疯狂的小聚会。

1128
00:52:06.770 --> 00:52:08.430
Ken Coop has directed our episode.
肯·库普导演了我们的这一集。

1129
00:52:08.970 --> 00:52:11.870
Nelson and I played writers in a writer's room.
纳尔逊和我在编剧室里演编剧。

1130
00:52:12.130 --> 00:52:13.070
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1131
00:52:13.070 --> 00:52:13.810
So funny.
太搞笑了。

1132
00:52:13.950 --> 00:52:16.030
And then Rashida plays Kenya's wife.
然后拉什达饰演肯尼亚的妻子。

1133
00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:18.230
And we all were there on the same day.
我们都在同一天去了现场。

1134
00:52:18.430 --> 00:52:19.670
Well, we had a blaSt.
总之，我们玩得很开心。

1135
00:52:19.810 --> 00:52:20.510
Nelson's great.
纳尔逊很棒。

1136
00:52:20.650 --> 00:52:22.130
I was excited he got to come back.
我很兴奋他能回归。

1137
00:52:22.310 --> 00:52:22.770
Me too.
我也是。

1138
00:52:22.770 --> 00:52:23.910
I really liked him.
我很喜欢他。

1139
00:52:24.090 --> 00:52:35.150
His character is going through our computers, and he's going to put up, like, blockers so that we can't waste time on certain websites.
他的角色在查我们的电脑，他还要设置拦截程序，这样我们就没法在某些网站上浪费时间了。

1140
00:52:35.510 --> 00:52:39.050
I mean, when he says YouTube, it looked like Michael pooped himself a little.
我是说，当他说到YouTube时，迈克尔看起来好像吓得快尿裤子了。

1141
00:52:39.450 --> 00:52:40.350
Very upset.
超级心烦。

1142
00:52:40.830 --> 00:52:42.750
But wait, there's more.
但等等，还有呢。

1143
00:52:43.070 --> 00:52:44.150
It doesn't stop there.
还没完呢。

1144
00:52:44.730 --> 00:52:47.390
Gabe has even more new policies.
盖布还有更多的新政策。

1145
00:52:48.050 --> 00:52:50.430
But before we do that, I think we should take a break.
但在我们讲那个之前，我想我们应该休息一下。

1146
00:52:50.570 --> 00:52:51.470
I need to use the restroom.
我要去趟洗手间。

1147
00:52:52.190 --> 00:52:52.490
Okay.
好的。

1148
00:52:53.410 --> 00:52:54.690
You're not going to argue with me.
你不会反对我的。

1149
00:52:54.750 --> 00:52:55.430
I appreciate it.
我很感激。

1150
00:52:55.510 --> 00:52:57.630
I will never argue with you for having to pee.
我绝不会因为你要小便而反对你。

1151
00:52:57.790 --> 00:52:58.750
You know this about me.
你了解我这一点的。

1152
00:52:58.910 --> 00:53:00.950
It's one of our company policies.
这是我们公司的政策之一。

1153
00:53:01.330 --> 00:53:02.650
Pee whenever you need to.
想上厕所的时候就去。

1154
00:53:02.730 --> 00:53:04.430
Go to the bathroom, you go to the bathroom.
去洗手间，你就去洗手间。

1155
00:53:04.450 --> 00:53:04.990
That's right.
没错。

1156
00:53:16.190 --> 00:53:17.190
We are back.
我们回来了。

1157
00:53:17.450 --> 00:53:18.710
My bladder is empty.
我的膀胱空了。

1158
00:53:19.010 --> 00:53:21.170
Your bladder is empty, and I ate half a donut.
你的膀胱空了，而我吃了一半甜甜圈。

1159
00:53:21.850 --> 00:53:23.350
So on brand for you, lady.
真符合你的作风，女士。

1160
00:53:23.570 --> 00:53:25.350
Someone brought donuts today.
今天有人带了甜甜圈来。

1161
00:53:25.610 --> 00:53:28.370
It was my happiest moment of my day so far.
这是我今天到目前为止最快乐的时刻。

1162
00:53:28.490 --> 00:53:29.670
But only half of it.
但只吃了一半。

1163
00:53:29.830 --> 00:53:31.190
You only ever eat half of anything.
你什么东西都只吃一半。

1164
00:53:31.490 --> 00:53:31.590
That's right.
没错。

1165
00:53:32.310 --> 00:53:33.030
Well, listen.
听着。

1166
00:53:33.190 --> 00:53:43.030
Gabe is in the conference room, and his next new announcement is that he is going to give each employee an aluminum Saber water bottle.
盖布在会议室里，他的下一个新公告是，他要给每个员工发一个铝制的塞伯水壶。

1167
00:53:43.030 --> 00:53:45.930
This is going to eliminate the need for plastic.
这将消除对塑料的需求。

1168
00:53:46.410 --> 00:53:48.330
It's going to be really good for the environment.
这对环境真的很好。

1169
00:53:48.630 --> 00:53:49.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1170
00:53:49.610 --> 00:53:52.570
But Michael is, like, upset.
但迈克尔好像很不高兴。

1171
00:53:53.030 --> 00:53:55.190
He's like, what about my little cups?
他说，那我那些小纸杯怎么办？

1172
00:53:55.190 --> 00:53:56.970
Like, my little cups I drink the water out of.
就是我用来喝水的那种小纸杯。

1173
00:53:56.970 --> 00:53:58.570
He drinks 20 a day.
他一天要用二十个。

1174
00:53:59.050 --> 00:54:01.390
Now, here's the thing that I think is kind of brilliant.
现在，我觉得有个地方挺聪明的。

1175
00:54:01.910 --> 00:54:06.810
Because Gabe says, I bet you can fit those 20 little cups into your water bottle.
因为盖布说，我打赌你绝对能把那二十个小纸杯塞进你的水壶里。

1176
00:54:06.810 --> 00:54:15.330
And Michael says, but what about the 20 little trips that I take to the water cooler each day where he scans the office?
然后迈克尔说，那我每天去饮水机那二十趟怎么办，顺便还能巡视办公室？

1177
00:54:15.530 --> 00:54:18.430
Or his 20 little conversations with Stanley.
或者他跟斯坦利的二十次闲聊怎么办。

1178
00:54:18.750 --> 00:54:19.430
Poor Stanley.
可怜的斯坦利。

1179
00:54:19.430 --> 00:54:21.150
Stanley's like, I can let go.
斯坦利心里想，我可算解脱了。

1180
00:54:21.610 --> 00:54:28.710
All this time, Stanley, like, unbeknownst to us, he's having 20 conversations a day with Michael.
一直以来，我们都不知道，斯坦利竟然一天要和迈克尔聊二十次。

1181
00:54:28.970 --> 00:54:30.410
Because he sits by the water cooler.
因为他的座位挨着饮水机。

1182
00:54:30.810 --> 00:54:33.690
I'm surprised he hasn't moved the water cooler, personally.
就我个人而言，我很惊讶他居然没把饮水机搬走。

1183
00:54:33.950 --> 00:54:36.290
That Stanley didn't move it, like, back into the annex.
惊讶斯坦利居然没把饮水机搬回附属办公室那边。

1184
00:54:36.490 --> 00:54:39.950
Or, I'm surprised Stanley hasn't requested to, like, trade seats with Creed.
或者，我惊讶斯坦利居然没有申请跟克里德换座位。

1185
00:54:40.650 --> 00:54:41.130
Truly.
真的。

1186
00:54:41.710 --> 00:54:43.890
Well, he likes his relationship with Phyllis.
好吧，他很享受和菲利斯的搭档关系。

1187
00:54:43.970 --> 00:54:44.550
We know that.
我们都知道这一点。

1188
00:54:44.770 --> 00:54:45.810
That's his work wife.
那是他的办公室工作妻子。

1189
00:54:45.950 --> 00:54:46.210
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1190
00:54:46.210 --> 00:54:49.330
I just want to say, I think it's actually a little genius.
我只想说，我觉得这其实有点天才。

1191
00:54:49.330 --> 00:54:53.470
The trip to the water cooler as a managerial technique.
把去饮水机当成一种管理手段。

1192
00:54:53.710 --> 00:54:55.510
I was like, oh, smart.
当时我就想，噢，真聪明。

1193
00:54:55.970 --> 00:54:59.330
If Michael really wanted to manage people, he just gets bored.
如果迈克尔真的想管理员工的话，他只是觉得无聊罢了。

1194
00:54:59.690 --> 00:55:00.470
That's true.
这倒也是。

1195
00:55:00.810 --> 00:55:02.910
Probably driven from another place.
大概是出于其他原因吧。

1196
00:55:03.150 --> 00:55:11.410
Well, at 7 minutes 28 seconds, if you look at the Sabre water bottle, that was made by Clean Canteen.
说到七分二十八秒，如果你看那个塞伯水壶，那是由Clean Canteen制造的。

1197
00:55:11.790 --> 00:55:12.230
Oh.
哦。

1198
00:55:12.470 --> 00:55:14.350
A little tidbit from Randy Cordray.
这是兰迪·科德雷提供的一个小花絮。

1199
00:55:14.350 --> 00:55:18.710
And they also applied the logo that was designed by Henry Sane.
而且他们还印上了由亨利·塞恩设计的标志。

1200
00:55:18.930 --> 00:55:24.770
I guess there were many, many variations of the Sabre logo that Greg and Paul had to choose from.
我猜格雷格和保罗当时必须从塞伯标志的许许多多版本中进行挑选。

1201
00:55:24.850 --> 00:55:25.930
And that's the one they picked.
这就是他们选中的那一个。

1202
00:55:26.590 --> 00:55:27.250
But, Jenna.
但是，珍娜。

1203
00:55:27.850 --> 00:55:28.170
Yeah?
嗯？

1204
00:55:28.470 --> 00:55:33.310
The whole time I was watching this scene, all I could remember was, we did this.
我整个过程在看这场戏时，脑子里唯一能想到的就是，我们做过这事。

1205
00:55:33.490 --> 00:55:34.590
We did this!
我们做过这事！

1206
00:55:34.730 --> 00:55:34.990
Yes!
对！

1207
00:55:35.110 --> 00:55:40.630
Paul Lieberstein made us all drink out of these canteens.
保罗·利伯斯坦让我们所有人用这些水壶喝水。

1208
00:55:40.630 --> 00:55:41.070
Yes!
对！

1209
00:55:41.290 --> 00:55:45.730
And I was like, wait, I know I have something in my digital clutter about this.
当时我就想，等等，我记得我的电子杂物里有关于这个的内容。

1210
00:55:45.950 --> 00:55:49.590
Some email saying that we were getting rid of plastic water bottles.
有封邮件说我们要停用塑料水瓶。

1211
00:55:49.750 --> 00:55:52.430
I knew I had something in my digital clutter about this.
我早知道我的数字杂物里有关于这个的东西。

1212
00:55:52.610 --> 00:55:53.010
Sam?
萨姆？

1213
00:55:55.550 --> 00:55:56.850
Angela's Digital Clutter.
安吉拉的电子杂物。

1214
00:55:58.550 --> 00:55:59.550
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1215
00:55:59.970 --> 00:56:05.310
So, Jenna, we all got an email during this time that there wouldn't be plastic water bottles on set.
所以，珍娜，当时我们都收到了一封邮件，说片场将不再提供塑料水瓶。

1216
00:56:05.470 --> 00:56:05.610
Yes, yes.
对，对。

1217
00:56:05.670 --> 00:56:09.330
That we were all getting a stainless steel water bottle.
说我们都会得到一个不锈钢水壶。

1218
00:56:09.470 --> 00:56:09.610
Yep.
没错。

1219
00:56:09.790 --> 00:56:11.270
That said Dunder Mifflin on it.
上面印着邓德米夫林。

1220
00:56:11.370 --> 00:56:11.550
Yep.
没错。

1221
00:56:11.690 --> 00:56:13.750
And we were going to refill them throughout the day.
而且我们整天都要用它们来接水。

1222
00:56:14.150 --> 00:56:16.810
So, Jenna, you remembered so quickly it was Paul.
所以，珍娜，你一下子就记起是保罗了。

1223
00:56:16.950 --> 00:56:22.530
I couldn't remember if it was Paul or Brent because I remember Brent was very much about being healthy and eco-friendly.
我记不清是保罗还是布伦特，因为我记得布伦特非常注重健康和环保。

1224
00:56:22.810 --> 00:56:23.010
Yes.
是的。

1225
00:56:23.010 --> 00:56:24.150
I texted Brent.
我给布伦特发了短信。

1226
00:56:24.290 --> 00:56:24.930
Brent, was this you?
布伦特，这是你搞的吗？

1227
00:56:25.050 --> 00:56:27.090
He was like, no, I'm pretty sure it was Paul.
他说，不，我挺确定是保罗。

1228
00:56:27.270 --> 00:56:31.710
So, then I emailed Paul and I said, Paul, I know we did this, right?
所以，我又给保罗发了邮件，我说，保罗，我知道我们做过这事，对吧？

1229
00:56:31.810 --> 00:56:34.050
I found in my digital clutter, was this your idea?
我在数字杂物里找到了，这是你的主意吗？

1230
00:56:34.230 --> 00:56:39.290
And was it also part of the inspiration for Gabe and his Saber water bottles?
这也是盖布和他的赛博水壶的灵感来源之一吗？

1231
00:56:39.470 --> 00:56:40.970
And this is what Paul had to say.
这就是保罗的回应。

1232
00:56:41.230 --> 00:56:45.130
Paul said, yes, I tried to get us to be plastic free.
保罗说，是的，我曾试图让我们做到无塑料。

1233
00:56:45.370 --> 00:56:46.630
It worked for a little while.
这管用了一小会儿。

1234
00:56:46.810 --> 00:56:48.150
I remember that, too.
我也记得。

1235
00:56:48.150 --> 00:56:49.630
It was very short-lived.
这维持的时间很短。

1236
00:56:49.630 --> 00:56:50.090
I know.
我知道。

1237
00:56:50.270 --> 00:56:58.030
He said, as far as it being an intended storyline for Gabe, he doesn't have a clear memory that that was specifically a Gabe storyline.
他说，至于这是否是给盖布安排的既定剧情线，他记不太清这具体是不是盖布的剧情了。

1238
00:56:58.030 --> 00:57:03.170
But in general, so much of what was happening around us was inspiration for the show.
但总体来说，我们身边发生的很多事情都成了节目的灵感来源。

1239
00:57:03.510 --> 00:57:04.090
All right.
好吧。

1240
00:57:04.270 --> 00:57:06.290
It was probably connected.
这可能是有联系的。

1241
00:57:06.450 --> 00:57:08.710
But I was like, oh, my gosh, we did this.
但我当时就想，哦，天哪，我们真的做过这事。

1242
00:57:09.170 --> 00:57:10.530
Do you know what I remembered?
你知道我记起什么了吗？

1243
00:57:10.870 --> 00:57:11.070
What?
什么？

1244
00:57:11.310 --> 00:57:12.970
I was standing in line to refill it.
我当时正排队去接水呢。

1245
00:57:13.150 --> 00:57:14.770
There literally was a line.
真的排了长队。

1246
00:57:14.870 --> 00:57:15.190
Yes.
对。

1247
00:57:15.190 --> 00:57:21.070
Well, you know, Paul told me that this was sort of a craze that was happening during this time.
嗯，你知道的，保罗告诉我，这可以说是那个时期的一种风潮。

1248
00:57:21.670 --> 00:57:24.630
Companies were really trying to limit plastic use.
当时各家公司都在极力限制塑料的使用。

1249
00:57:24.790 --> 00:57:27.790
And so he wanted us to be a part of that, you know?
所以他想让我们也成为其中的一部分，你知道吗？

1250
00:57:27.790 --> 00:57:28.150
Yes.
是的。

1251
00:57:28.270 --> 00:57:30.070
I do think it's a great idea.
我的确觉得这是个好主意。

1252
00:57:30.710 --> 00:57:34.930
But I think you need more than one refill jug area.
但我觉得你们需要不止一个加水区。

1253
00:57:35.290 --> 00:57:36.990
That probably would have helped.
那可能确实会有所帮助。

1254
00:57:37.030 --> 00:57:37.790
That would have helped.
那确实会有帮助。

1255
00:57:39.330 --> 00:57:49.270
Well, Michael has a talking head about all this, where he says, okay, there's a small part of him that's excited about the new company, but 70% of him is water.
嗯，迈克尔对此有一段单人访谈，在访谈中他说，好吧，他内心有一小部分为新公司感到兴奋，但他的百分之七十是水。

1256
00:57:49.590 --> 00:57:55.090
And at the end of this talking head, he says that he thinks these changes suck ball.
而在这段访谈结束时，他说他觉得这些改变真他妈烂透了。

1257
00:57:56.070 --> 00:57:57.670
Because you know what he was going to say.
因为你知道他本来要说什么。

1258
00:57:57.990 --> 00:57:58.790
Sucks balls.
烂透了。

1259
00:57:59.010 --> 00:57:59.790
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1260
00:57:59.790 --> 00:58:05.030
I guess cutting off the end of Michael saying balls was an idea that John had.
我猜剪掉迈克尔说“球”字的那句话是约翰想出来的点子。

1261
00:58:05.190 --> 00:58:07.630
He came up with it in editing with Dave Rogers.
这是他和剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯在后期制作中想出来的。

1262
00:58:07.830 --> 00:58:09.990
And I love their take on this.
我很喜欢他们对这部分的看法。

1263
00:58:10.130 --> 00:58:14.090
So what they were saying was that obviously Michael completed his sentence.
所以他们的意思是，迈克尔很明显把句子说完了。

1264
00:58:14.650 --> 00:58:22.950
But they imagined that when the documentary aired, that the documentarians would have left in all of the footage.
但他们想象当纪录片播出时，纪录片制作团队会保留所有的素材。

1265
00:58:23.130 --> 00:58:27.330
But the network running the documentary would have to cut it off.
但播出这部纪录片的电视台必须把它剪掉。

1266
00:58:27.490 --> 00:58:28.050
Right.
对啊。

1267
00:58:28.050 --> 00:58:30.550
Because of, you know, standards and practices.
因为，你知道的，审查标准和规范。

1268
00:58:30.550 --> 00:58:38.390
And he said they based that on the amount of times that we had to cut things or change things because of standards and practices.
他说他们是根据我们因为审查标准和规范而必须剪掉或修改内容的次数来做出这种假设的。

1269
00:58:38.850 --> 00:58:40.250
Every episode, probably.
大概每一集都有吧。

1270
00:58:40.490 --> 00:58:41.310
Very realistic.
非常现实。

1271
00:58:41.850 --> 00:58:46.490
Well, listen, Angela, you mentioned the line to fill their water bottles.
好吧，听着，安吉拉，你提到了排队接水的那句台词。

1272
00:58:46.690 --> 00:58:50.270
And while Michael is in line, Toby's getting water and it runs out.
就在迈克尔排队的时候，托比正在接水，然后水刚好用完了。

1273
00:58:50.390 --> 00:58:53.270
Toby says we kicked it, which cracked me up.
托比说我们把它喝光了，这让我笑得前仰后合。

1274
00:58:53.350 --> 00:58:53.830
Me too.
我也是。

1275
00:58:53.830 --> 00:58:56.670
I wrote it down at 8 minutes, 45 seconds.
我把它记下来了，在8分45秒的时候。

1276
00:58:57.210 --> 00:58:59.570
That's what you say when a keg runs out, right?
那是当一桶啤酒喝光时你会说的话，对吧？

1277
00:58:59.650 --> 00:59:00.150
I know.
我知道。

1278
00:59:00.810 --> 00:59:02.870
Well, what does that tell us about Toby?
那么，这说明了托比的什么情况呢？

1279
00:59:03.230 --> 00:59:05.370
Well, I think what does it tell us about Paul?
好吧，我觉得这说明了保罗的什么情况？

1280
00:59:05.710 --> 00:59:10.330
Because I've bought a pony keg with Paul and we've kicked it.
因为我和保罗买过一小桶啤酒，而且我们把它喝光了。

1281
00:59:10.550 --> 00:59:16.070
See, I would never use that language because I've never purchased a keg and I've never had a beer out of a keg.
你看，我绝不会用那种说法，因为我从来没买过一桶啤酒，也从来没从酒桶里喝过啤酒。

1282
00:59:16.070 --> 00:59:17.030
Oh, man.
天哪。

1283
00:59:17.410 --> 00:59:18.210
I'm not a beer person.
我对啤酒无感。

1284
00:59:18.550 --> 00:59:18.770
Listen.
听着。

1285
00:59:19.110 --> 00:59:23.670
Now, I'll do a flavored ale or a cider beer.
现在，我会喝调味艾尔啤酒或者西打啤酒。

1286
00:59:23.950 --> 00:59:29.310
A really, really cold keg and like getting a beer out of a super cold keg.
一桶非常非常冰的啤酒，就像从超冰的酒桶里倒出一杯啤酒一样。

1287
00:59:29.330 --> 00:59:31.250
It's great, especially like on a hot day.
感觉棒极了，特别是在炎热的日子里。

1288
00:59:31.250 --> 00:59:35.830
Maybe you put one, you know, at second base because you're playing softball with friends.
也许你会在二垒放一个，你知道的，因为你在和朋友们打垒球。

1289
00:59:35.830 --> 00:59:42.310
And if you make it to second base, you get a beer and you get a little tooted while you're waiting to run into home plate.
如果你上了二垒，你就能喝上一杯啤酒，在等待跑回本垒的过程中还能微醺一会儿。

1290
00:59:42.730 --> 00:59:45.350
That cold beer out of a keg.
从酒桶里倒出的那杯冰啤酒。

1291
00:59:45.450 --> 00:59:46.290
It's amazing.
简直太棒了。

1292
00:59:46.290 --> 00:59:48.470
I mean, that sounds miserable to me.
我的意思是，听起来对我来说简直是折磨。

1293
00:59:48.690 --> 00:59:52.570
You drink some beer and then you have to run on your sloshy beer stomach.
你喝了些啤酒，然后还得挺着个满是晃荡啤酒的胃去跑步。

1294
00:59:52.910 --> 00:59:57.230
Have you seen like co-ed softball like with a group of friends?
你看过那种和一群朋友一起玩的男女混合垒球赛吗？

1295
00:59:57.390 --> 00:59:58.830
This is not like real athleticism.
这可算不上什么真正的运动精神。

1296
00:59:58.830 --> 01:00:01.590
You have lived part of life that I haven't lived.
你经历过我未曾经历过的人生。

1297
01:00:01.990 --> 01:00:03.750
You've had all these experiences.
你经历过所有这些体验。

1298
01:00:04.130 --> 01:00:07.570
And to me, it's like you lived in a foreign land.
对我和来说，这就好像你曾在异国他乡生活过一样。

1299
01:00:08.090 --> 01:00:08.390
What?
什么？

1300
01:00:08.590 --> 01:00:10.730
A foreign land of softball and beer?
充满垒球和啤酒的异国他乡吗？

1301
01:00:10.970 --> 01:00:11.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1302
01:00:11.590 --> 01:00:14.990
I have no like frame of reference for that.
我完全没有这方面的参照概念。

1303
01:00:14.990 --> 01:00:17.490
I know you and Lee bond over this stuff all the time.
我知道你和李经常因为这些事情产生共鸣。

1304
01:00:17.610 --> 01:00:18.670
Is this a Texas thing?
这是德克萨斯的特色吗？

1305
01:00:18.870 --> 01:00:20.430
I mean, I'm sure they're doing it in Missouri.
我的意思是，密苏里肯定也有人这么做。

1306
01:00:20.490 --> 01:00:21.410
Where was I?
我刚才说到哪了？

1307
01:00:21.510 --> 01:00:23.190
What was I doing during this time?
这段时间我在干什么？

1308
01:00:23.190 --> 01:00:26.810
This was just like a hip young person out in the world.
这就像是个赶时髦的年轻人四处闯荡。

1309
01:00:26.810 --> 01:00:28.430
I've never been a hip young person.
我可从来没当过赶时髦的年轻人。

1310
01:00:28.530 --> 01:00:29.150
Well, that's true.
嗯，这倒是真的。

1311
01:00:29.250 --> 01:00:32.150
I've been a 65-year-old woman since the day I was born.
我从出生那一天起就像个六十五岁的老太太。

1312
01:00:32.290 --> 01:00:32.770
It's true.
千真万确。

1313
01:00:32.770 --> 01:00:33.850
And I love you for it.
我就是喜欢你这样。

1314
01:00:33.890 --> 01:00:34.510
Thank you, lady.
谢谢你，女士。

1315
01:00:34.810 --> 01:00:37.590
As I stare at your big fake flower that's on your lapel.
当我盯着你翻领上那朵硕大的假花时。

1316
01:00:37.590 --> 01:00:38.890
I know it's not working.
我知道它不管用。

1317
01:00:38.890 --> 01:00:40.630
I know it's not working.
我知道它根本不管用。

1318
01:00:44.990 --> 01:00:47.430
This cannot happen on our book launch tour.
这绝对不能在我们的新书签售巡回活动中发生。

1319
01:00:47.870 --> 01:00:48.850
It can't.
绝对不行。

1320
01:00:48.970 --> 01:00:49.450
Look at me.
看着我。

1321
01:00:49.530 --> 01:00:50.330
It's ridiculous.
这太荒谬了。

1322
01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:51.610
You never had to.
你从来不需要。

1323
01:00:51.610 --> 01:00:53.250
Is water coming out of this flower?
这朵花里会喷水吗？

1324
01:00:53.450 --> 01:00:54.190
Squirt, squirt.
喷水，喷水。

1325
01:00:54.330 --> 01:00:55.670
It's borderline clownish.
这简直有点像小丑了。

1326
01:00:55.830 --> 01:00:56.650
It can't happen.
这绝不能发生。

1327
01:00:56.890 --> 01:00:58.690
You never had to prove it to me.
你从来都不需要向我证明。

1328
01:00:59.350 --> 01:01:01.150
I've known it from the beginning.
我从一开始就知道。

1329
01:01:01.370 --> 01:01:03.590
Well, I needed to prove it to myself.
好吧，我需要向自己证明。

1330
01:01:04.070 --> 01:01:04.790
All right.
好吧。

1331
01:01:04.990 --> 01:01:05.950
Where are we?
我们到哪了？

1332
01:01:06.370 --> 01:01:10.050
Well, Toby has just kicked the water cooler.
哦，托比刚刚踢了饮水机。

1333
01:01:10.050 --> 01:01:11.570
Oh, yes, that's right.
噢，对，没错。

1334
01:01:11.890 --> 01:01:14.110
Well, now Michael's going to confront Gabe.
好了，现在迈克尔要去找加布对质了。

1335
01:01:14.450 --> 01:01:18.710
He's going to say, listen, I don't mean to seem ungrateful, but I am really struggling
他会说，听着，我不是故意显得不知感恩，但我真的很挣扎

1336
01:01:18.710 --> 01:01:21.770
to embrace some of these changes, such as all of them.
去接受这些改变中的任何一部分，比如所有的改变。

1337
01:01:23.490 --> 01:01:26.090
Gabe says it's kind of above his pay grade.
加布说这超出了他的职责权限。

1338
01:01:26.390 --> 01:01:31.190
He can't really change any of the policies, but he'll see what he can do.
他其实无法改变任何政策，但他会看看能做些什么。

1339
01:01:31.670 --> 01:01:36.870
And now Pam and Jim are going to enter the daycare center.
现在帕姆和吉姆要走进托儿所了。

1340
01:01:36.870 --> 01:01:40.790
All of these scenes were absolutely delicious.
所有这些场景都太精彩了。

1341
01:01:41.010 --> 01:01:43.090
I loved watching them.
我特别喜欢看。

1342
01:01:43.350 --> 01:01:45.390
We had a fan question from Alice R.
我们收到了来自意大利

1343
01:01:45.490 --> 01:01:45.930
in Italy.
的爱丽丝·R的粉丝提问。

1344
01:01:46.190 --> 01:01:48.490
Where did you shoot the daycare scenes?
你们是在哪里拍摄托儿所场景的？

1345
01:01:48.630 --> 01:01:49.950
Was it a real daycare?
那是真正的托儿所吗？

1346
01:01:50.210 --> 01:01:51.790
Did you make any changes?
你们做什么改动了吗？

1347
01:01:52.730 --> 01:01:54.570
Lady, did you recognize it?
蕾迪，你认出来了吗？

1348
01:01:54.930 --> 01:01:55.490
No.
没有。

1349
01:01:56.110 --> 01:01:56.390
Okay.
好吧。

1350
01:01:56.410 --> 01:01:58.850
Well, it's called Sandbox Daycare.
嗯，它叫沙盒托儿所。

1351
01:01:58.850 --> 01:01:59.730
We made that up.
那是我们编的。

1352
01:01:59.930 --> 01:02:02.030
That's not even a real daycare in Scranton.
那甚至都不是斯克兰顿真正的日托中心。

1353
01:02:02.490 --> 01:02:06.550
We shot this at Peekaboo Playland in Eagle Rock, California.
我们是在加利福尼亚州鹰岩的“躲猫猫游乐园”拍的。

1354
01:02:06.870 --> 01:02:09.610
Did you not take Isabel to Peekaboo Playland?
你没带伊莎贝尔去过躲猫猫游乐园吗？

1355
01:02:09.690 --> 01:02:11.990
Was that after she was a toddler?
那是她过了幼儿期之后吗？

1356
01:02:12.290 --> 01:02:14.810
This was all the rage when my kids were little.
我孩子小的时候，这可风靡一时了。

1357
01:02:15.150 --> 01:02:16.490
Eagle Rock's far from me.
鹰岩离我挺远的。

1358
01:02:16.690 --> 01:02:17.750
I guess that's true.
倒也是。

1359
01:02:17.790 --> 01:02:23.150
We had tons and tons of Playland-type places right by me, so I never needed to venture
我住处附近有数不清的这种游乐场所，所以我从来不需要跑这么远

1360
01:02:23.150 --> 01:02:23.710
this far.
来这里。

1361
01:02:23.930 --> 01:02:26.770
Well, you know, when I did this episode, I didn't have kids.
嗯，你知道的，我拍这一集的时候还没孩子。

1362
01:02:26.770 --> 01:02:29.790
But then when I was re-watching it, I was like, it's Peekaboo!
但后来重看的时候，我就想，这不是躲猫猫嘛！

1363
01:02:29.930 --> 01:02:31.270
It's Peekaboo Playland!
这就是躲猫猫游乐园！

1364
01:02:31.270 --> 01:02:34.850
I've spent so many days in this space!
我在这地方度过了好多天！

1365
01:02:34.850 --> 01:02:36.790
See, the one by me is the Coop.
你看，我常去的那家叫“鸡舍”。

1366
01:02:36.930 --> 01:02:38.670
I spent tons of time at the Coop.
我在“鸡舍”度过了大量时间。

1367
01:02:38.770 --> 01:02:39.710
I've been to the Coop.
我去过“鸡舍”。

1368
01:02:39.850 --> 01:02:40.030
Yeah.
对。

1369
01:02:40.590 --> 01:02:40.890
All right.
好吧。

1370
01:02:41.010 --> 01:02:43.490
So there's a big twirly slide in the middle.
所以中间有一个很大的旋转滑梯。

1371
01:02:43.790 --> 01:02:46.670
There's like a treehouse around the curly slide.
