但你如何避免把其他所有东西都吸进去？

1987
01:30:41.800 --> 01:30:42.880
You just suck it.
你只要吸一下就行了。

1988
01:30:43.000 --> 01:30:43.900
You just suck it.
你只要吸一下就行了。

1989
01:30:44.000 --> 01:30:44.560
You just suck it.
你只要吸一下就行了。

1990
01:30:45.960 --> 01:30:48.580
Well, Michael's going to leave David Wallace's.
好吧，迈克尔要离开大卫·华莱士家了。

1991
01:30:48.660 --> 01:30:50.240
He's so defeated.
他太受挫了。

1992
01:30:50.680 --> 01:30:54.320
He says very few things would make him say no to working with David Wallace,
他说很少有事情会让他拒绝和大卫·华莱士合作，

1993
01:30:54.460 --> 01:30:55.840
but suck it is one of them.
但“吸它”就是其中之一。

1994
01:30:55.840 --> 01:31:04.540
And then I love this shot of Michael slowly pulling away and David Wallace is sort of like
然后我喜欢这个镜头，迈克尔慢慢把车开走，而大卫·华莱士有点像

1995
01:31:04.540 --> 01:31:09.940
lumbering down the driveway toward the car, like kind of like a zombie.
笨拙地沿着车道朝汽车走去，有点像个僵尸。

1996
01:31:10.140 --> 01:31:11.980
It reminded me of a zombie movie.
这让我想起了僵尸电影。

1997
01:31:13.060 --> 01:31:15.940
Jen Salata said this shot was John's idea,
珍·萨拉塔说这个镜头是约翰的主意，

1998
01:31:15.940 --> 01:31:19.720
and I think it is some foreshadowing for A Quiet Place.
而且我认为这有点像《寂静之地》的伏笔。

1999
01:31:19.840 --> 01:31:20.440
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

2000
01:31:20.500 --> 01:31:21.220
I really do.
我真的是这么觉得。

2001
01:31:21.220 --> 01:31:22.880
It felt very horror movie to me.
我觉得这非常有恐怖片的感觉。

2002
01:31:23.160 --> 01:31:28.560
Right after this creepy goodbye with David Wallace would have come the final accounting scene
在跟大卫·华莱士那段诡异的告别之后，本来应该有一场最终的会计部戏码

2003
01:31:28.560 --> 01:31:30.520
in the runner that got deleted.
也就是被删掉的那段走廊戏。

2004
01:31:31.140 --> 01:31:32.940
Here's how it wraps up.
结局是这样的。

2005
01:31:33.360 --> 01:31:35.440
Accounting area, interior office.
会计部区域，办公室内部。

2006
01:31:35.760 --> 01:31:37.740
Angela's looking over Kevin's work.
安吉拉正在检查凯文的工作。

2007
01:31:37.980 --> 01:31:39.760
Angela, who did this?
安吉拉：“这是谁干的？”

2008
01:31:40.080 --> 01:31:41.340
Oscar shakes his head.
奥斯卡摇了摇头。

2009
01:31:41.860 --> 01:31:44.820
Kevin, it's possible I did it on my own.
凯文：“安吉拉，这可能是我自己做的。”

2010
01:31:45.180 --> 01:31:47.240
Angela, no, it's not.
安吉拉：“不，不可能。”

2011
01:31:47.600 --> 01:31:50.200
That is the one thing that is not possible.
“唯独这绝对不可能。”

2012
01:31:50.200 --> 01:31:51.460
How did this happen?
“这到底是怎么回事？”

2013
01:31:52.240 --> 01:31:53.920
Kevin, I did it.
凯文：“安吉拉，是我干的。”

2014
01:31:54.620 --> 01:31:56.960
Angela sighs, confused, and walks away.
安吉拉叹了口气，一脸困惑地走开了。

2015
01:31:57.140 --> 01:32:00.840
Just missing Todd, who approaches with Kevin's adding machine.
正好跟托德擦肩而过，托德拿着凯文的加法机走了过来。

2016
01:32:01.180 --> 01:32:02.320
Kevin looks nervous.
凯文显得很紧张。

2017
01:32:02.960 --> 01:32:05.200
Todd, you left this on my desk.
托德：“你把这个落在我的桌上了。”

2018
01:32:05.540 --> 01:32:06.500
Kevin, thanks.
凯文：“谢谢。”

2019
01:32:07.000 --> 01:32:09.400
Todd and Oscar ad-lib hellos.
托德和奥斯卡即兴打了个招呼。

2020
01:32:09.740 --> 01:32:10.840
And Todd leaves.
然后托德离开了。

2021
01:32:11.380 --> 01:32:13.380
Kevin, don't tell Angela.
凯文：“别告诉安吉拉。”

2022
01:32:13.800 --> 01:32:15.260
Oscar, I won't.
奥斯卡：“我不会的。”

2023
01:32:15.640 --> 01:32:18.140
Kevin, I didn't just let him do the work.
凯文：“我可不只是让他帮我干活。”

2024
01:32:18.260 --> 01:32:19.020
I learned stuff.
“我学到了东西。”

2025
01:32:19.020 --> 01:32:20.140
Please don't tell her.
“求你别告诉她。”

2026
01:32:20.700 --> 01:32:22.360
Oscar, I said I won't.
奥斯卡：“我都说我不会了。”

2027
01:32:22.920 --> 01:32:23.940
Kevin looks nervous.
凯文显得很紧张。

2028
01:32:24.460 --> 01:32:25.520
Oscar looks up at him.
奥斯卡抬头看着他。

2029
01:32:25.940 --> 01:32:28.620
Oscar, he trained me when I started here.
奥斯卡：“我刚来这里的时候，是他培训的我。”

2030
01:32:29.100 --> 01:32:30.160
Kevin, really?
凯文：“真的吗？”

2031
01:32:30.500 --> 01:32:32.660
Oscar nods, and Kevin smiles.
奥斯卡点点头，凯文笑了。

2032
01:32:33.240 --> 01:32:35.720
What a sweet ending to that story.
这个故事的结局真是太温馨了。

2033
01:32:35.940 --> 01:32:38.700
I know, and who is Todd at Vance Refrigeration?
我知道，万斯冷冻公司的托德是谁啊？

2034
01:32:38.900 --> 01:32:43.520
I mean, it kind of sounded like maybe Todd used to work at Dunder Mifflin?
我是说，听起来好像托德以前在邓德米夫林工作过？

2035
01:32:43.700 --> 01:32:44.320
I don't know.
我不知道。

2036
01:32:44.320 --> 01:32:45.920
I feel like Todd is training people.
我感觉托德一直在培训别人。

2037
01:32:46.840 --> 01:32:47.040
Yeah.
是啊。

2038
01:32:47.720 --> 01:32:49.580
Anyway, I thought that was sort of sweet.
不管怎样，我觉得那挺温馨的。

2039
01:32:49.920 --> 01:32:54.800
Well, speaking of sweet, something we haven't talked about is that cutie pie scene at reception
说到温馨，我们还没聊过的一幕是前台安迪和亚伦那场可爱的小戏码

2040
01:32:54.800 --> 01:32:59.640
with Andy and Aaron, where they're both not asking each other out on a date.
他们俩谁也没有约对方出去。

2041
01:32:59.640 --> 01:33:07.700
It's a totally adorable scene, but if I'm being honest, I was very distracted by the fact that Pam's watercolor is back on the wall.
那场戏真的超级可爱，但老实说，我完全被另一件事吸引了注意力，那就是潘的水彩画又挂回墙上了。

2042
01:33:07.780 --> 01:33:08.540
It's all I could see.
我眼里就只有那个。

2043
01:33:09.320 --> 01:33:10.320
It's all I could see.
我眼里就只有那个。

2044
01:33:10.320 --> 01:33:11.400
I was just so delighted.
我当时真的太高兴了。

2045
01:33:12.300 --> 01:33:14.720
Michael's going to return, and he's going to make a toaSt.
迈克尔要回来了，他还要发表祝酒词。

2046
01:33:14.900 --> 01:33:16.520
He's brought a lot of orange juice.
他带了好多橙汁。

2047
01:33:16.580 --> 01:33:19.200
I guess in honor of Tallahassee.
我猜是为了向塔拉哈西致敬。

2048
01:33:19.480 --> 01:33:19.920
Florida.
佛罗里达。

2049
01:33:20.300 --> 01:33:20.520
Yeah.
对。

2050
01:33:20.820 --> 01:33:21.260
Oranges.
橙子。

2051
01:33:21.760 --> 01:33:22.940
He makes his toaSt.
他举杯祝酒。

2052
01:33:23.100 --> 01:33:27.520
It's not really a toast, but everyone takes a big swig, and they're like, ugh.
其实不算什么祝酒，但每个人都猛灌了一大口，然后都觉得，呃。

2053
01:33:28.120 --> 01:33:33.240
Yeah, I mean, have you ever had orange juice out of, like, an aluminum container?
对啊，我是说，你喝过用铝制容器装的橙汁吗？

2054
01:33:33.560 --> 01:33:34.360
A little tangy.
有点刺鼻。

2055
01:33:34.880 --> 01:33:38.500
Yeah, I mean, it goes right into your teeth, just like they talk about.
是啊，我是说，就像他们说的那样，直接渗进你的牙齿里。

2056
01:33:38.700 --> 01:33:39.700
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

2057
01:33:39.700 --> 01:33:44.080
I don't think that a lot of people are putting their orange juice into metal containers.
我觉得没多少人会把橙汁装进金属容器里。

2058
01:33:44.080 --> 01:33:46.540
You know, it's really meant to be a water vessel.
你知道的，那本来就是个水容器。

2059
01:33:46.980 --> 01:33:48.440
I like that you said vessel.
我喜欢你用了“容器”这个词。

2060
01:33:48.680 --> 01:33:49.200
Thank you.
谢谢。

2061
01:33:49.400 --> 01:33:50.720
It's a water vessel.
这就是个水容器。

2062
01:33:50.880 --> 01:33:51.460
It is.
确实是的。

2063
01:33:51.780 --> 01:33:54.500
Well, I guess this toast means that Michael is going to stay.
好吧，我猜这个祝酒意味着迈克尔要留下来了。

2064
01:33:54.680 --> 01:33:56.260
He's going to stick it out at Saber.
他要坚持留在萨博公司。

2065
01:33:56.260 --> 01:33:56.900
He is.
他会的。

2066
01:33:57.000 --> 01:34:01.120
He's going to, I guess, have to abide by all these new rules that he hates.
我猜他得遵守所有那些他讨厌的新规矩。

2067
01:34:01.300 --> 01:34:03.460
No YouTube for Michael at work?
迈克尔在工作时不能看YouTube了？

2068
01:34:03.720 --> 01:34:05.120
I don't know how that's going to go.
我不知道这会变成什么样。

2069
01:34:05.320 --> 01:34:09.900
The episode ends with David Wallace and his son jamming out to a song that he's written
这一集的结尾是大卫·华莱士和他的儿子即兴演奏了他写的一首歌

2070
01:34:09.900 --> 01:34:10.740
called Suck It.
歌名叫《吸干它》。

2071
01:34:10.920 --> 01:34:12.060
Let's listen to it.
我们来听听看。

2072
01:34:48.640 --> 01:34:50.440
Oh, and Daniel's on the druMs.
哦，而且丹尼尔在打鼓。

2073
01:34:50.440 --> 01:34:51.220
I know, man.
我知道，老兄。

2074
01:34:51.840 --> 01:34:55.940
We got a fan question from Donna in Newport, New Virginia.
我们收到了来自弗吉尼亚州纽波特的唐娜的粉丝提问。

2075
01:34:55.940 --> 01:35:01.560
Please tell us everything about the Suck It song at the end of the episode, How Much
请给我们讲讲剧集结尾那首《吸干它》的所有事情，究竟有多少

2076
01:35:01.560 --> 01:35:02.640
Was Improvised.
是即兴创作的。

2077
01:35:03.100 --> 01:35:09.500
I will tell you, Donna, the lyrics to Suck It were written by Warren and Halstead.
我来告诉你，唐娜，《吸干它》的歌词是由沃伦和霍尔斯特德写的。

2078
01:35:09.680 --> 01:35:12.880
These guys really were our go-to guys for song lyrics.
这些人确实是我们写歌词的御用人选。

2079
01:35:13.620 --> 01:35:17.640
And then I reached out to Andy Buckley, who plays David Wallace.
然后我联系了饰演大卫·华莱士的安迪·巴克利。

2080
01:35:17.640 --> 01:35:22.980
He said that Warren and Halstead faxed him the lyrics the night before.
他说沃伦和霍尔斯特德在头天晚上把歌词传真给了他。

2081
01:35:23.600 --> 01:35:25.060
Old tech alert, Angela.
旧科技警报，安吉拉。

2082
01:35:25.300 --> 01:35:25.720
Fax.
传真。

2083
01:35:25.880 --> 01:35:26.220
Yeah.
是的。

2084
01:35:26.440 --> 01:35:27.460
They faxed them.
他们发了传真。

2085
01:35:27.820 --> 01:35:29.360
He went over them that night.
他那天晚上把歌词过了一遍。

2086
01:35:29.500 --> 01:35:31.540
He went over them at lunch the next day.
第二天午休时他又过了一遍。

2087
01:35:31.700 --> 01:35:34.860
That's when he was able to kind of fiddle around on a keyboard.
就在那时，他得以在电子琴上随便弹奏了一会儿。

2088
01:35:35.320 --> 01:35:39.620
Andy said he only knew about three chords on a keyboard.
安迪说他在电子琴上只懂大约三个和弦。

2089
01:35:39.620 --> 01:35:41.320
But he did his beSt.
但他尽了最大努力。

2090
01:35:41.740 --> 01:35:44.260
They did not shoot this until the very end of the day.
他们直到一天的最后才拍摄这一幕。

2091
01:35:44.400 --> 01:35:47.460
They only had three minutes before they went into overtime.
他们离加班只有三分钟时间了。

2092
01:35:47.780 --> 01:35:48.880
Three minutes?
三分钟？

2093
01:35:49.200 --> 01:35:49.480
Yes.
是的。

2094
01:35:49.760 --> 01:35:50.900
No messing up.
不容许出错。

2095
01:35:51.020 --> 01:35:51.520
Yes.
是的。

2096
01:35:51.760 --> 01:35:55.520
He said it all came together when Owen started playing the druMs.
他说当欧文开始打鼓时，一切都融合到了一起。

2097
01:35:55.760 --> 01:35:57.260
It was kind of a magic moment.
这有点像是一个魔幻时刻。

2098
01:35:57.700 --> 01:35:59.420
They got it in three takes.
他们拍了三条就过了。

2099
01:35:59.800 --> 01:36:02.620
He said that the whole shoot day was a total blaSt.
他说整个拍摄日过得太开心了。

2100
01:36:02.620 --> 01:36:04.380
He loved John as a director.
他很喜欢作为导演的约翰。

2101
01:36:04.680 --> 01:36:07.480
He said John just had tons of positive energy.
他说约翰浑身充满积极的能量。

2102
01:36:07.480 --> 01:36:10.660
And that John and Jen Salata worked so well together.
而且约翰和詹·萨拉塔合作得非常默契。

2103
01:36:10.880 --> 01:36:14.120
He sort of remembered that someone would do a take.
他依稀记得有人会拍一个镜头。

2104
01:36:14.140 --> 01:36:16.300
And then you'd see them kind of huddle and giggle.
然后你会看到他们聚在一起嘀咕、咯咯笑。

2105
01:36:16.480 --> 01:36:18.460
And then they would come over with some great idea.
接着他们就会带着某个绝妙的点子走过来。

2106
01:36:18.700 --> 01:36:19.740
That's my memory, too.
这也是我的记忆。

2107
01:36:19.940 --> 01:36:20.180
Same.
我也是。

2108
01:36:20.620 --> 01:36:27.380
Andy said that inevitably, if he is walking through an airport or some public place,
安迪说，难免地，如果他走过机场或某个公共场所，

2109
01:36:27.760 --> 01:36:29.920
there is always someone who yells out,
总会有人大喊一声，

2110
01:36:30.060 --> 01:36:30.680
Suck it!
去你的吧！

2111
01:36:32.760 --> 01:36:39.550
He said that he and Zach Woods are now on an HBO comedy called
他说他和扎克·伍兹现在正在拍一部HBO的喜剧叫

2112
01:36:39.550 --> 01:36:42.290
Avenue 5, and it films in London.
《第五大道》，在伦敦拍摄。

2113
01:36:42.530 --> 01:36:43.110
Amazing.
太棒了。

2114
01:36:43.510 --> 01:36:48.490
He said they were in London for four months before the pandemic in the summer of 2019,
他说在2019年夏天的疫情爆发前，他们在伦敦待了四个月，

2115
01:36:48.490 --> 01:36:52.130
and they just went back this past fall in 2021.
然后在2021年刚过去的那个秋天又回去了。

2116
01:36:52.950 --> 01:36:59.050
He said that the difference between people stopping the two of them before the pandemic
他说，疫情前人们拦住他们两个的这种情况，

2117
01:36:59.050 --> 01:37:01.430
and after the pandemic is striking.
与疫情后相比形成了鲜明的对比。

2118
01:37:01.430 --> 01:37:06.250
He said, clearly, a lot of people binged The Office during the pandemic.
他说，很显然，许多人在疫情期间疯狂刷了《办公室》。

2119
01:37:06.550 --> 01:37:09.610
He's getting way more suckets lately.
他最近听到“去你的吧”的频率高得多了。

2120
01:37:10.050 --> 01:37:11.830
Well, I hope that's a good thing.
嗯，我希望这是件好事。

2121
01:37:12.050 --> 01:37:12.710
I think so.
我想是的。

2122
01:37:13.410 --> 01:37:15.150
Well, that is the Saber episode.
好啦，这就是那集《塞伯》。

2123
01:37:15.510 --> 01:37:20.450
Well, before we go, I thought we could end this episode with a few final thoughts from John
那么，在结束之前，我想我们可以用约翰的一些最后感悟来结束这集，

2124
01:37:20.450 --> 01:37:23.650
about what directing this episode meant to him.
谈谈执导这一集对他的意义。

2125
01:37:24.510 --> 01:37:27.190
This show was my film school.
这部剧就是我的电影学院。

2126
01:37:27.490 --> 01:37:30.510
I mean, I was a waiter before I got the show.
我是说，在加入这部剧之前我只是个服务生。

2127
01:37:30.690 --> 01:37:35.850
I had zero experience in this business, in anything, acting, writing, directing, producing,
我对这个行业零经验，无论是表演、编剧、导演、制片，

2128
01:37:36.170 --> 01:37:36.890
any of that stuff.
还是别的什么。

2129
01:37:37.610 --> 01:37:39.890
And there it was, right in front of me.
而它就这样呈现在我眼前。

2130
01:37:39.890 --> 01:37:48.130
I was somehow lucky enough to drop right into the most immense pool of talent that I could
我不知怎么地非常幸运，一头扎进了我所能要求的、最庞大的人才池里，

2131
01:37:48.130 --> 01:37:55.930
ever ask for from that insane group of people that we had as our writers, a group of people
那是由我们那群疯狂的编剧组成的团队，我想，

2132
01:37:55.930 --> 01:37:59.190
that hadn't been assembled like that in a long, long time, I guess.
那样的一群人已经很久很久没有集结在一起了。

2133
01:37:59.390 --> 01:38:01.950
And, you know, in a lot of ways, probably hasn't been assembled since.
而且，你知道，从很多方面来说，可能之后再也没有集结过。

2134
01:38:01.950 --> 01:38:09.710
So from writing, I got to understand what it meant to not only write well, but to have
所以从编剧方面，我开始明白不仅要写得好意味着什么，

2135
01:38:09.710 --> 01:38:13.110
fun with it and to have this drive to do something great.
还要从中获得乐趣，并怀揣着做成伟大之事的动力。

2136
01:38:13.370 --> 01:38:18.070
I remember going up to the writers rooms every now and again, if I had a break between scenes
我记得只要场景之间有空隙什么的，我就会时不时去编剧室，

2137
01:38:18.070 --> 01:38:22.130
or something and, you know, watch them all come up with an idea.
你知道的，看他们所有人想出一个点子。

2138
01:38:22.130 --> 01:38:27.830
And the idea was almost like you could visualize a balloon in the air and 12 to 14 people were
那个点子就像你能想象空中飘着一个气球，12到14个人

2139
01:38:27.830 --> 01:38:32.710
making sure it didn't touch the ground before they had investigated every single possibility
确保它不落地，直到他们把每一种可能性能不能行得通、

2140
01:38:32.710 --> 01:38:37.310
of how to make it work and how to make a joke work or an idea work.
能不能让一个笑话或一个点子奏效的方式都研究透彻。

2141
01:38:37.810 --> 01:38:42.270
And even if it didn't end up working, they still put it on a different board that was like,
即使最后行不通，他们也会把它贴在另一块板上，

2142
01:38:42.330 --> 01:38:45.070
well, it's not working today, but maybe it'll work again on another day.
就好像，好吧，今天不行，但改天说不定就行了。

2143
01:38:45.310 --> 01:38:51.770
And if it did work, they all work together to try to figure out how it would best be used
如果确实行得通，他们就会齐心协力想办法

2144
01:38:51.770 --> 01:38:52.690
in this show.
怎样才能在这部剧中发挥出最好的效果。

2145
01:38:52.690 --> 01:38:59.070
So writing wise, there I was front row seats in the greatest room I could be visually.
所以在编剧方面，我坐在前排观众席，身处我能亲眼见证的最好的房间里。

2146
01:38:59.070 --> 01:39:02.570
I had no idea what even a camera was.
我甚至不知道什么是摄像机。

2147
01:39:02.690 --> 01:39:05.070
I didn't know what the difference between lenses were.
我不知道镜头之间有什么区别。

2148
01:39:05.310 --> 01:39:11.730
I didn't know what type of cameras did what, but I remember there again, the office was shot
我不知道什么类型的摄像机有什么作用，但我记得，还是那句话，《办公室》是用

2149
01:39:11.730 --> 01:39:12.970
single camera.
单机位拍摄的。

2150
01:39:13.130 --> 01:39:16.570
It was one of the first shows to be done and like that in a long time.
它是很久以来第一批采用这种方式拍摄的剧集之一。

2151
01:39:16.830 --> 01:39:19.590
And so we were shooting the show like a movie.
所以我们当时拍这部剧就像拍电影一样。

2152
01:39:19.590 --> 01:39:25.910
So I got to pick the brain of Randall and Matt and all these hugely talented people who
因此我有机会向伦道夫、马特以及所有这些极具才华的人请教，

2153
01:39:25.910 --> 01:39:32.050
would explain to me everything from lenses to the aesthetic and lighting and all these
他们会向我解释一切，从镜头到美学、灯光，以及所有这些

2154
01:39:32.050 --> 01:39:34.430
different things that I had absolutely no idea about.
我以前完全一无所知的事情。

2155
01:39:34.670 --> 01:39:39.270
After directing Saber, I used to hang out with Dave Rogers and watch him cut all these
在执导完《Saber》之后，我经常和戴夫·罗杰斯混在一起，看他剪辑所有这些

2156
01:39:39.270 --> 01:39:39.850
different episodes.
不同的剧集。

2157
01:39:39.850 --> 01:39:44.250
I'd pop in and see how he was making all these scenes work, how he was rearranging story,
我会顺便去看看他是如何让这些场景发挥作用的，他是如何重新调整故事的，

2158
01:39:44.250 --> 01:39:49.470
how he was taking air out of a moment to make it work so much stronger.
他是如何在一个瞬间中留白，让它产生更强烈的效果的。

2159
01:39:49.870 --> 01:39:56.450
So really, at the end of the day, I certainly would not be writing and directing at all if
所以说到底，如果不是因为这部剧，

2160
01:39:56.450 --> 01:39:57.350
it wasn't for this show.
我绝对不可能去进行编剧和导演工作。

2161
01:39:57.490 --> 01:39:59.830
I just I wouldn't have had the confidence to do it.
我就是不会有自信去这么做。

2162
01:39:59.930 --> 01:40:05.630
So I guess what I'm trying to say is I owe absolutely everything to this show.
所以我想说的是，我的一切都完全归功于这部剧。

2163
01:40:06.230 --> 01:40:12.950
Directing this episode was so very special and I will truly never forget it.
执导这一集是如此特别，我真的永远不会忘记。

2164
01:40:12.950 --> 01:40:15.090
Thank you for having me on the show.
谢谢你们邀请我参加这个节目。

2165
01:40:15.510 --> 01:40:19.210
I was so excited to come back and have me back again.
我非常高兴能回来，并再次邀请我。

2166
01:40:19.770 --> 01:40:21.510
But again, like I said, slow down.
但再说一次，就像我说的，放慢节奏。

2167
01:40:21.750 --> 01:40:23.210
We need more of this podcast, please.
我们还需要更多这样的播客，拜托了。

2168
01:40:24.190 --> 01:40:25.790
John Krasinski, we love you.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基，我们爱你。

2169
01:40:26.010 --> 01:40:27.410
Love you so much, John.
非常爱你，约翰。

2170
01:40:27.610 --> 01:40:29.450
That was so generous of you.
你真是太大方了。

2171
01:40:29.670 --> 01:40:33.410
You shared so much with us and I just loved hearing your voice.
你和我们分享了那么多，我真的很喜欢听你的声音。

2172
